  ('jurisdiction', 'DC', '2026-11-22T02:26:12Z'::timestamptz, 'official_text', 'verified', 'https://dob.dc.gov/node/1613981', null, 'The 2017 DC Construction Codes consist of the 2015 International Code Council (ICC) family of model codes, the 2014 National Electrical Code, and 2013 ASHRAE 90.1, as amended by the District of Columbia Municipal Regulations (DCMR) Title 12, Sections A through M. The 2017 DC Construction Code takes effect on May 29, 2020.', 'Statewide code model, re-checked on the official page.'),
  ('adoption', (md5('academykb:adoption:st:DE:iecc:2024')::uuid)::text, '2026-11-22T02:26:12Z'::timestamptz, 'official_text', 'verified', 'https://documents.dnrec.delaware.gov/Admin/Orders/Secretarys-Order-No-2026-CCE-0002.pdf', '11452132d0fedf1644c769fbdacb041b8ab86e274ba8b16e932fc9e3d83ce6bb', 'Secretary’s Order No.: 2026-CCE-0002 RE: Approving Final Regulations to Amend 7 DE Admin. Code 2101: Regulations for State Energy Conservation Code Date of Issuance: March 10, 2026 Effective Date of the Amendment: April 11, 2026 ... Promulgation of the revised proposed amendments to 7 DE Admin. Code 2101: Regulations for State Energy Conservation Code will enable the Department to adopt by reference the 2024 IECC for residential buildings, the 2024 IECC/ASHRAE 90.1- 2022 for commercial and high-rise residential buildings, and Appendix RE: EV Charging Infrastructure and Appendix CB: Solar-Ready Zone, with amendments;', 'Quote re-checked word for word on the official page by the Academy source check.'),
  ('adoption', (md5('academykb:adoption:st:DE:ashrae_90_1:2022')::uuid)::text, '2026-11-22T02:26:12Z'::timestamptz, 'official_text', 'verified', 'https://documents.dnrec.delaware.gov/Admin/Orders/Secretarys-Order-No-2026-CCE-0002.pdf', '11452132d0fedf1644c769fbdacb041b8ab86e274ba8b16e932fc9e3d83ce6bb', 'Secretary’s Order No.: 2026-CCE-0002 RE: Approving Final Regulations to Amend 7 DE Admin. Code 2101: Regulations for State Energy Conservation Code Date of Issuance: March 10, 2026 Effective Date of the Amendment: April 11, 2026 ... Promulgation of the revised proposed amendments to 7 DE Admin. Code 2101: Regulations for State Energy Conservation Code will enable the Department to adopt by reference the 2024 IECC for residential buildings, the 2024 IECC/ASHRAE 90.1- 2022 for commercial and high-rise residential buildings, and Appendix RE: EV Charging Infrastructure and Appendix CB: Solar-Ready Zone, with amendments;', 'Quote re-checked word for word on the official page by the Academy source check.'),
  ('adoption', (md5('academykb:adoption:st:DE:ipc:2021')::uuid)::text, '2026-11-22T02:26:12Z'::timestamptz, 'official_text', 'verified', 'https://archive.regulations.delaware.gov/AdminCode/title16/Department%20of%20Health%20and%20Social%20Services/Division%20of%20Public%20Health/Health%20Systems%20Protection%20(HSP)/4455.shtml', 'd1d537e6e2d6e94fbe9605a40234bd33855fea0b37b46cb2a1bd0655dfc9a797', 'The Delaware Division of Public Health shall hereby adopt the 2021 International Plumbing Code with following amendments. The code shall be known as the "2021 State of Delaware Plumbing Code" . Every political subdivision within the State, including county, city, or municipal governments, shall enforce the International Plumbing Code (IPC) as adopted or modified by the Division of Public Health.', 'Quote re-checked word for word on the official page by the Academy source check.'),
  ('adoption', (md5('academykb:adoption:st:DE:nfpa1:2024')::uuid)::text, '2026-11-22T02:26:12Z'::timestamptz, 'official_text', 'verified', 'https://statefiremarshal.delaware.gov/wp-content/uploads/sites/110/2025/12/2026-DSFPR-update.pdf', '60ef5999406e06b41ed24608a2d21baa9df89ace614b804f2467b8875ba68e1c', 'The State Fire Prevention Commission has recently adopted a new edition of the Delaware State Fire Prevention Regulations, Regulation 701, which becomes effective January 1, 2026. ... Regulation 701, Chapter 7 of the Delaware State Fire Prevention Regulations has a complete list of the NFPA Codes and Standards that will be effective January 1, 2026. Some of the commonly used include: • NFPA 1, Fire Code, 2024 edition.', 'Quote re-checked word for word on the official page by the Academy source check.'),
  ('jurisdiction', 'DE', '2026-11-22T02:26:12Z'::timestamptz, 'official_text', 'verified', 'https://delcode.delaware.gov/title16/c076/index.html', null, 'The Levy Court of Kent County and the County Councils of New Castle County and Sussex County may adopt and enforce building codes, plumbing codes, electrical codes or other similar codes.', 'Statewide code model, re-checked on the official page.'),
  ('jurisdiction', 'FL', '2026-11-22T02:26:12Z'::timestamptz, 'official_text', 'verified', 'https://www.leg.state.fl.us/statutes/index.cfm?App_mode=Display_Statute&URL=0500-0599/0553/Sections/0553.73.html', null, '(6) The initial adoption of, and any subsequent update or amendment to, the Florida Building Code by the commission is deemed adopted for use statewide without adoptions by local government.', 'Statewide code model, re-checked on the official page.'),
  ('adoption', (md5('academykb:adoption:st:GA:ibc:2024')::uuid)::text, '2026-11-22T02:26:12Z'::timestamptz, 'official_text', 'verified', 'https://dca.georgia.gov/document/document/new-codes-and-amendments-effective-january-1-2026-memo/download', '050ac9e001d9ae23f6406a427938cd688826d43b2df28a257066b9ead9ce85a5', 'The Georgia Department of Community Affairs (DCA) Board, upon recommendation of the State Codes Advisory Committee (SCAC), voted to adopt the following codes with an effective date of January 1, 2026: ... 2024 International Building Code with Georgia Amendments', 'Quote re-checked word for word on the official page by the Academy source check.'),
  ('adoption', (md5('academykb:adoption:st:GA:irc:2024')::uuid)::text, '2026-11-22T02:26:12Z'::timestamptz, 'official_text', 'verified', 'https://dca.georgia.gov/document/document/new-codes-and-amendments-effective-january-1-2026-memo/download', '050ac9e001d9ae23f6406a427938cd688826d43b2df28a257066b9ead9ce85a5', 'voted to adopt the following codes with an effective date of January 1, 2026: ... 2024 International Residential Code with Georgia Amendments', 'Quote re-checked word for word on the official page by the Academy source check.'),
  ('adoption', (md5('academykb:adoption:st:GA:ipc:2024')::uuid)::text, '2026-11-22T02:26:12Z'::timestamptz, 'official_text', 'verified', 'https://dca.georgia.gov/document/document/new-codes-and-amendments-effective-january-1-2026-memo/download', '050ac9e001d9ae23f6406a427938cd688826d43b2df28a257066b9ead9ce85a5', 'voted to adopt the following codes with an effective date of January 1, 2026: ... 2024 International Plumbing Code with Georgia Amendments', 'Quote re-checked word for word on the official page by the Academy source check.'),
  ('adoption', (md5('academykb:adoption:st:GA:imc:2024')::uuid)::text, '2026-11-22T02:26:12Z'::timestamptz, 'official_text', 'verified', 'https://dca.georgia.gov/document/document/new-codes-and-amendments-effective-january-1-2026-memo/download', '050ac9e001d9ae23f6406a427938cd688826d43b2df28a257066b9ead9ce85a5', 'voted to adopt the following codes with an effective date of January 1, 2026: ... 2024 International Mechanical Code with Georgia Amendments', 'Quote re-checked word for word on the official page by the Academy source check.'),
  ('adoption', (md5('academykb:adoption:st:GA:ifgc:2024')::uuid)::text, '2026-11-22T02:26:12Z'::timestamptz, 'official_text', 'verified', 'https://dca.georgia.gov/document/document/new-codes-and-amendments-effective-january-1-2026-memo/download', '050ac9e001d9ae23f6406a427938cd688826d43b2df28a257066b9ead9ce85a5', 'voted to adopt the following codes with an effective date of January 1, 2026: ... 2024 International Fuel Gas Code with Georgia Amendments', 'Quote re-checked word for word on the official page by the Academy source check.'),
  ('adoption', (md5('academykb:adoption:st:GA:nec:2023')::uuid)::text, '2026-11-22T02:26:12Z'::timestamptz, 'official_text', 'verified', 'https://dca.georgia.gov/document/document/new-codes-and-amendments-effective-january-1-2026-memo/download', '050ac9e001d9ae23f6406a427938cd688826d43b2df28a257066b9ead9ce85a5', 'voted to adopt the following codes with an effective date of January 1, 2026: • 2026 Georgia Amendments to the 2023 National Electrical Code', 'Quote re-checked word for word on the official page by the Academy source check.'),
  ('adoption', (md5('academykb:adoption:st:GA:iecc:2015')::uuid)::text, '2026-11-22T02:26:12Z'::timestamptz, 'official_text', 'verified', 'https://dca.georgia.gov/document/publications/iecc2020amendmentspdf/download', 'a0112e7a0f389a569108ac7b824f315984b8d961053ee4824cd5ecdb8ba0290d', 'The INTERNATIONAL ENERGY CONSERVATION CODE, 2015 Edition, published by the International Code Council, when used in conjunction with these Georgia State Supplements and Amendments and any other Georgia State Amendments, shall constitute the official Georgia State Minimum Standard Energy Code.', 'Quote re-checked word for word on the official page by the Academy source check.'),
  ('adoption', (md5('academykb:adoption:st:GA:iebc:2018')::uuid)::text, '2026-11-22T02:26:12Z'::timestamptz, 'official_text', 'verified', 'https://dca.georgia.gov/community-assistance/construction-codes/current-state-minimum-codes-construction', '058398fa151ac00dd2236b62b2847ba7ad7dcfff2cc8979680cb94c4588f7ef6', 'Current Permissive Codes as Adopted by DCA International Property Maintenance Code, 2018 Edition, with Georgia Amendments ... International Existing Building Code, 2018 Edition, with Georgia Amendments', 'Quote re-checked word for word on the official page by the Academy source check.'),
  ('jurisdiction', 'GA', '2026-11-22T02:26:12Z'::timestamptz, 'official_text', 'verified', 'https://dca.georgia.gov/community-assistance/construction-codes/mandatory-and-permissive-state-codes', null, 'As noted above, the building, one and two family dwelling residential, fire, plumbing, mechanical, gas, electrical, energy, and swimming pool codes are mandatory codes, meaning that under Georgia law, any structure built in Georgia must comply with these codes, whether or not the local government chooses to locally enforce these codes.', 'Statewide code model, re-checked on the official page.'),
  ('adoption', (md5('academykb:adoption:st:HI:irc:2018')::uuid)::text, '2026-11-22T02:26:12Z'::timestamptz, 'official_text', 'verified', 'https://ags.hawaii.gov/bcc/files/2021/09/2018StateResidentialCode_20201117rev1.pdf', 'dd50bb0e1f98be39716fca7bbcce076b3fc4f05517ae998020d49765facbce91', 'Adopting the 2018 International Residential Code with Amendments The attached document is the Hawaii State Residential Code as adopted on November 17, 2020 by the State Building Code Council in accordance with HRS 107-24.', 'Quote re-checked word for word on the official page by the Academy source check.'),
  ('adoption', (md5('academykb:adoption:st:HI:ibc:2018')::uuid)::text, '2026-11-22T02:26:12Z'::timestamptz, 'official_text', 'verified', 'https://ags.hawaii.gov/bcc/files/2021/09/2018StateBuildingCode_20210817.pdf', '304f88574eceb66626792f124a714e4cdeecc61d4a642e583d997f6a59c3ffe5', 'Adopting the 2018 International Building Code with Amendments The attached document is the Hawaii State Building Code as adopted on April 20, 2021 by the State Building Code Council in accordance with HRS 107-24.', 'Quote re-checked word for word on the official page by the Academy source check.'),
  ('adoption', (md5('academykb:adoption:st:HI:iebc:2018')::uuid)::text, '2026-11-22T02:26:12Z'::timestamptz, 'official_text', 'verified', 'https://ags.hawaii.gov/bcc/files/2021/09/2018StateExistingBuildingCode_20201117.pdf', '1ba01b64cba860f210bf12fc62c54eca63c8e6ca0a7950122e7220761120ad52', 'Adopting the 2018 International Existing Building Code with Amendments The attached document is the Hawaii State Existing Building Code as adopted on November 17, 2020 by the State Building Code Council in accordance with HRS 107-24.', 'Quote re-checked word for word on the official page by the Academy source check.'),
  ('adoption', (md5('academykb:adoption:st:HI:iecc:2018')::uuid)::text, '2026-11-22T02:26:12Z'::timestamptz, 'official_text', 'verified', 'https://ags.hawaii.gov/bcc/files/2021/01/soh_bcc_energycode_20201215.pdf', 'dabe1e2007a6a0fb2049435af4c975bfaa7fd844decbefff822ffce8b9e88e98', 'The attached document is the Hawai‘i State Energy Code Amendments to the 2018 IECC as adopted on December 15, 2020 by the State Building Code Council in accordance with HRS 107-24. ... Effective Date: December 15, 2020', 'Quote re-checked word for word on the official page by the Academy source check.'),
  ('adoption', (md5('academykb:adoption:st:HI:nfpa1:2024')::uuid)::text, '2026-11-22T02:26:12Z'::timestamptz, 'official_text', 'verified', 'https://law.hawaii.gov/wp-content/uploads/2025/09/NFPA1-2024-Hawaii-State-Fire-Code-amendments.pdf', 'f29b6bcd095a4380fe3ff7da7ec231def8ea64b1b53582938b2cbe6e62588dfe', 'HAWAII STATE FIRE CODE Effective Date: September 5, 2025 ... 4. Adoption of the 2024 NFPA 1, Fire Code. The NFPA 1, Fire Code, 2024 edition is adopted (incorporated by reference), subject to the amendments provided in this chapter.', 'Quote re-checked word for word on the official page by the Academy source check.'),
  ('jurisdiction', 'HI', '2026-11-22T02:26:12Z'::timestamptz, 'official_text', 'verified', 'https://ags.hawaii.gov/bcc/files/2021/09/2018StateBuildingCode_20210817.pdf', null, 'No later than April 20, 2023, each county in the State of Hawaii must amend and adopt the attached code in accordance with HRS 107-28(a). If by April 20, 2023, a county does not amend the attached code, it shall become applicable as an interim county building code in accordance with HRS 107-28(b).', 'Statewide code model, re-checked on the official page.'),
  ('adoption', (md5('academykb:adoption:st:IA:ibc:2024')::uuid)::text, '2026-11-22T02:26:12Z'::timestamptz, 'official_text', 'verified', 'https://www.legis.iowa.gov/docs/iac/chapter/11-19-2026.481.301.pdf', 'fe15db7f44408859cadaa8d50db81661431ecbe902356b41c03925ec101ca9cd', '481—301.3(103A) General provisions. The provisions of the International Building Code, 2024 edition, published by the International Code Council, www.iccsafe.org, are hereby adopted by reference as the general requirements for building construction ... [ARC 9474C, IAB 8/6/25, effective 9/10/25; Editorial change: IAC Supplement 11/26/25]', 'Quote re-checked word for word on the official page by the Academy source check.'),
  ('adoption', (md5('academykb:adoption:st:IA:irc:2024')::uuid)::text, '2026-11-22T02:26:12Z'::timestamptz, 'official_text', 'verified', 'https://www.legis.iowa.gov/docs/iac/chapter/11-19-2026.481.301.pdf', 'fe15db7f44408859cadaa8d50db81661431ecbe902356b41c03925ec101ca9cd', '481—301.8(103A) Residential construction requirements. The provisions of the International Residential Code, 2024 edition, published by the International Code Council, located at www.iccsafe.org, are hereby adopted by reference as the requirements for construction, alteration, movement, enlargement, replacement, repair, equipment, use and occupancy, location, removal, and demolition of detached one- and two-family dwellings ... [ARC 9474C, IAB 8/6/25, effective 9/10/25; Editorial change: IAC Supplement 11/26/25]', 'Quote re-checked word for word on the official page by the Academy source check.'),
  ('adoption', (md5('academykb:adoption:st:IA:iebc:2024')::uuid)::text, '2026-11-22T02:26:12Z'::timestamptz, 'official_text', 'verified', 'https://www.legis.iowa.gov/docs/iac/chapter/11-19-2026.481.301.pdf', 'fe15db7f44408859cadaa8d50db81661431ecbe902356b41c03925ec101ca9cd', '481—301.7(103A) Existing buildings. The provisions of the International Existing Building Code, 2024 edition, published by the International Code Council, located at www.iccsafe.org, are hereby adopted by reference as the requirements for repair, alteration, change of occupancy, addition, and relocation of existing buildings ... [ARC 9474C, IAB 8/6/25, effective 9/10/25; Editorial change: IAC Supplement 11/26/25]', 'Quote re-checked word for word on the official page by the Academy source check.'),
  ('adoption', (md5('academykb:adoption:st:IA:iecc:2012')::uuid)::text, '2026-11-22T02:26:12Z'::timestamptz, 'official_text', 'verified', 'https://www.legis.iowa.gov/docs/iac/chapter/11-19-2026.481.301.pdf', 'fe15db7f44408859cadaa8d50db81661431ecbe902356b41c03925ec101ca9cd', '481—301.24(103A) Residential energy code. The International Energy Conservation Code – Residential Provisions, 2012 edition, published by the International Code Council, located at www.iccsafe.org, is adopted by reference as the residential energy code of the state of Iowa building code, applicable to residential construction limited to three or fewer stories throughout the state of Iowa', 'Quote re-checked word for word on the official page by the Academy source check.'),
  ('adoption', (md5('academykb:adoption:st:IA:iecc:2012')::uuid)::text, '2026-11-22T02:26:12Z'::timestamptz, 'official_text', 'verified', 'https://www.legis.iowa.gov/docs/iac/chapter/11-19-2026.481.301.pdf', 'fe15db7f44408859cadaa8d50db81661431ecbe902356b41c03925ec101ca9cd', '481—301.25(103A) Adoption of nonresidential energy code. The International Energy Conservation Code – Commercial Provisions, 2012 edition, published by the International Code Council, located at www.iccsafe.org, is hereby adopted by reference as the nonresidential energy code of the state building code, applicable to commercial construction or residential construction of four or more stories within the state of Iowa', 'Quote re-checked word for word on the official page by the Academy source check.'),
  ('adoption', (md5('academykb:adoption:st:IA:upc:2024')::uuid)::text, '2026-11-22T02:26:12Z'::timestamptz, 'official_text', 'verified', 'https://www.legis.iowa.gov/docs/iac/chapter/11-19-2026.481.425.pdf', 'b2c6cbf1e233495acbd3b27aa1b237ec05287913797a98797355893602aa0d03', '481—425.1(105) Adoption. Sections 101 and 102, Chapters 2 to 17 and Appendices A and M of the Uniform Plumbing Code (UPC), 2024 Edition ... are hereby adopted by reference with amendments as the state plumbing code authorized by Iowa Code section 105.4. ... [ARC 8913C, IAB 2/19/25, effective 3/26/25; Editorial change: IAC Supplement 4/2/25] 481—425.2(105) Applicability. ... Local jurisdictions may not adopt other plumbing codes. Local jurisdictions may adopt additional amendments provided they are stricter', 'Quote re-checked word for word on the official page by the Academy source check.'),
  ('adoption', (md5('academykb:adoption:st:IA:imc:2024')::uuid)::text, '2026-11-22T02:26:12Z'::timestamptz, 'official_text', 'verified', 'https://www.legis.iowa.gov/docs/iac/chapter/11-19-2026.481.426.pdf', '5811bae5ecc239542add837cbdf53027b5f2d16b83ec999a6ff88a998e210fb2', '481—426.2(105) Adoption by reference. Sections 101 and 102 and Chapters 2 through 15 of the International Mechanical Code, 2024 edition, published by the International Code Council, www.iccsafe.org, are hereby adopted by reference as the requirements for the design, installation, maintenance, alteration, and inspection of mechanical systems ... within buildings and premises in Iowa. [ARC 8914C, IAB 2/19/25, effective 3/26/25; Editorial change: IAC Supplement 4/2/25]', 'Quote re-checked word for word on the official page by the Academy source check.'),
  ('adoption', (md5('academykb:adoption:st:IA:nec:2023')::uuid)::text, '2026-11-22T02:26:12Z'::timestamptz, 'official_text', 'verified', 'https://www.legis.iowa.gov/docs/iac/chapter/11-19-2026.481.404.pdf', 'c81ca81484453b7a6d782c030c9723b964e9494a00d5942163b88a781d97a673', '481—404.3(103) Installation requirements. The provisions of the National Electrical Code, 2023 edition, published by the National Fire Protection Association, are incorporated herein by reference as the requirements for electrical installations performed by persons subject to licensing and inspection pursuant to Iowa Code chapter 103 ... [ARC 9033C, IAB 3/19/25, effective 7/1/25; Editorial change: IAC Supplement 7/9/25]', 'Quote re-checked word for word on the official page by the Academy source check.'),
  ('adoption', (md5('academykb:adoption:st:IA:ifc:2024')::uuid)::text, '2026-11-22T02:26:12Z'::timestamptz, 'official_text', 'verified', 'https://www.legis.iowa.gov/docs/iac/chapter/11-19-2026.481.280.pdf', '9bf6227ab95324652d1f9130859520fd796dedfe2ce7449774ab031b7ed2bf00', '481—280.8(10A) General provisions. The following publications or indicated portions thereof are hereby adopted by reference as general fire safety requirements and apply to all occupancies ... 280.8(1) International Fire Code, 2024 edition, published by the International Code Council ... [ARC 9472C, IAB 8/6/25, effective 9/10/25; Editorial change: IAC Supplement 11/26/25; ARC 0246D, IAB 4/29/26, effective 6/3/26]', 'Quote re-checked word for word on the official page by the Academy source check.'),
  ('jurisdiction', 'IA', '2026-11-22T02:26:12Z'::timestamptz, 'official_text', 'verified', 'https://www.legis.iowa.gov/docs/code/103A.10.pdf', null, '2. The state building code shall be applicable: a. To all buildings and structures owned by the state or an agency of the state. b. In each governmental subdivision where the governing body has enacted an ordinance accepting the application of the code. c. To all newly constructed buildings and structures the construction of which is paid for in whole or in part with moneys appropriated by the state but which are not wholly owned by the state.', 'Statewide code model, re-checked on the official page.'),
  ('adoption', (md5('academykb:adoption:st:ID:ibc:2018')::uuid)::text, '2026-11-22T02:26:12Z'::timestamptz, 'official_text', 'verified', 'https://adminrules.idaho.gov/rules/current/24/243930.pdf', 'f44bb50bc6b4cba0deaaad5714feac3aeff1545ec43e347fa481e4b970809fa9', '01. International Building Code. The 2018 Edition, including appendices pertaining to building accessibility, with the following amendments: (7-1-24)', 'Quote re-checked word for word on the official page by the Academy source check.'),
  ('adoption', (md5('academykb:adoption:st:ID:irc:2018')::uuid)::text, '2026-11-22T02:26:12Z'::timestamptz, 'official_text', 'verified', 'https://adminrules.idaho.gov/rules/current/24/243930.pdf', 'f44bb50bc6b4cba0deaaad5714feac3aeff1545ec43e347fa481e4b970809fa9', '03. International Residential Code, 2018 Edition. Parts I, II, III, and IX of the 2018 Edition for one (1)- and two (2)- family dwellings, with the following amendments: (7-1-24)', 'Quote re-checked word for word on the official page by the Academy source check.'),
  ('adoption', (md5('academykb:adoption:st:ID:iebc:2018')::uuid)::text, '2026-11-22T02:26:12Z'::timestamptz, 'official_text', 'verified', 'https://adminrules.idaho.gov/rules/current/24/243930.pdf', 'f44bb50bc6b4cba0deaaad5714feac3aeff1545ec43e347fa481e4b970809fa9', '04. International Existing Building Code. 2018 Edition. (7-1-24)', 'Quote re-checked word for word on the official page by the Academy source check.'),
  ('adoption', (md5('academykb:adoption:st:ID:iecc:2018')::uuid)::text, '2026-11-22T02:26:12Z'::timestamptz, 'official_text', 'verified', 'https://adminrules.idaho.gov/rules/current/24/243930.pdf', 'f44bb50bc6b4cba0deaaad5714feac3aeff1545ec43e347fa481e4b970809fa9', '05. International Energy Conservation Code – Commercial Provisions. The 2018 Edition with the following amendments: (7-1-24)', 'Quote re-checked word for word on the official page by the Academy source check.'),
  ('adoption', (md5('academykb:adoption:st:ID:iecc:2018')::uuid)::text, '2026-11-22T02:26:12Z'::timestamptz, 'official_text', 'verified', 'https://adminrules.idaho.gov/rules/current/24/243930.pdf', 'f44bb50bc6b4cba0deaaad5714feac3aeff1545ec43e347fa481e4b970809fa9', '06. International Energy Conservation Code – Residential Provisions. The 2018 Edition with the following amendments: (7-1-24)', 'Quote re-checked word for word on the official page by the Academy source check.'),
  ('adoption', (md5('academykb:adoption:st:ID:imc:2018')::uuid)::text, '2026-11-22T02:26:12Z'::timestamptz, 'official_text', 'verified', 'https://adminrules.idaho.gov/rules/current/24/243970.pdf', '61c864fea77e602cbe97036dd5f939d6aca8749a021c2f6b6b156c26be898562', 'Pursuant to Section 54-5001, Idaho Code, the Board adopts, as the Idaho Mechanical Code, the following international codes with identified amendments: (3-28-23) 01. International Mechanical Code. The 2018 Edition, including appendix A, with the following amendments:', 'Quote re-checked word for word on the official page by the Academy source check.'),
  ('adoption', (md5('academykb:adoption:st:ID:ifgc:2018')::uuid)::text, '2026-11-22T02:26:12Z'::timestamptz, 'official_text', 'verified', 'https://adminrules.idaho.gov/rules/current/24/243970.pdf', '61c864fea77e602cbe97036dd5f939d6aca8749a021c2f6b6b156c26be898562', '02. International Fuel Gas Code. The 2018 Edition, including appendices A, B, C, and D, with the following amendments:', 'Quote re-checked word for word on the official page by the Academy source check.'),
  ('adoption', (md5('academykb:adoption:st:ID:upc:2015')::uuid)::text, '2026-11-22T02:26:12Z'::timestamptz, 'official_text', 'verified', 'https://adminrules.idaho.gov/rules/current/24/243920.pdf', '8c8531e6c48dc2d0dd12dcfdc77b907b4cd54f417b49362dbc3813ae025402f9', 'Pursuant to Section 54-2601, Idaho Code, the Board adopts, as the Idaho State Plumbing Code (ISPC), the 2015 Uniform Plumbing Code, including Appendices A, B, C, D, E, G, I, J, K and L, with the following amendments: (3-28-23)', 'Quote re-checked word for word on the official page by the Academy source check.'),
  ('adoption', (md5('academykb:adoption:st:ID:nec:2023')::uuid)::text, '2026-11-22T02:26:12Z'::timestamptz, 'official_text', 'verified', 'https://adminrules.idaho.gov/rules/current/24/243910.pdf', '08cac7210db4a3906729e8ffc9d8a3c4523b18d4de1c69bf55461c8d911f304a', '01. Documents. Under the provisions of Section 54-1001, Idaho Code, the National Electrical Code, 2023 Edition, (herein NEC) is amended as follows: (4-4-25)', 'Quote re-checked word for word on the official page by the Academy source check.'),
  ('adoption', (md5('academykb:adoption:st:ID:ifc:2018')::uuid)::text, '2026-11-22T02:26:12Z'::timestamptz, 'official_text', 'verified', 'https://dopl.idaho.gov/wp-content/uploads/2025/06/2025-Updated-Idaho-Adopted-Codes.pdf', '672aef6827dd860d0ec6bd8683240bebf592d4fd4f4d8c7a9e297d92a81f45a4', 'Fire Code (administered by the Idaho State Fire Marshal): 2018 International Fire Code', 'Quote re-checked word for word on the official page by the Academy source check.'),
  ('jurisdiction', 'ID', '2026-11-22T02:26:12Z'::timestamptz, 'official_text', 'verified', 'https://legislature.idaho.gov/statutesrules/idstat/Title39/T39CH41/SECT39-4109/', null, '(1) The following codes are hereby adopted for the state of Idaho division of occupational and professional licenses and shall only be applied by local governments as prescribed by section 39-4116, Idaho Code:', 'Statewide code model, re-checked on the official page.'),
  ('adoption', (md5('academykb:adoption:st:IL:iecc:2024')::uuid)::text, '2026-11-22T02:26:12Z'::timestamptz, 'official_text', 'verified', 'https://cdb.illinois.gov/business/codes/illinois-energy-codes/illinois-energy-conservation-code.html', '47fe304dbfda36b4f690378cc4843500ba254a3b704d7eee4f504e177932c944', 'Residential Buildings must comply with Illinois Energy Conservation Code per 20 ILCS 3125. See Subpart D of the Illinois Energy Code for more information. The 2024 edition of the IECC as amended went into effect on 11/30/25.', 'Quote re-checked word for word on the official page by the Academy source check.'),
  ('adoption', (md5('academykb:adoption:st:IL:ibc:ibc-iebc-current-or-most-recent-preceding-edition-')::uuid)::text, '2026-11-22T02:26:12Z'::timestamptz, 'official_text', 'verified', 'https://cdb.illinois.gov/business/codes/buildingcodesregulations.html', 'b893845507294f1554cd5d3c7899e063df67f5b4a71f852b7d5805d8aa537438', 'Commercial buildings in jurisdictions that have not adopted a building code AND state funded buildings. New or substantially improved buildings: IEBC © and IBC © (1/1/25 Incl. App G., Excl. Ch 11, 13, 29). Current edition or most recent preceeding edition.', 'Quote re-checked word for word on the official page by the Academy source check.'),
  ('adoption', (md5('academykb:adoption:st:IL:nec:nec-current-or-most-recent-preceding-edition-for-c')::uuid)::text, '2026-11-22T02:26:12Z'::timestamptz, 'official_text', 'verified', 'https://cdb.illinois.gov/business/codes/buildingcodesregulations.html', 'b893845507294f1554cd5d3c7899e063df67f5b4a71f852b7d5805d8aa537438', 'Excl. Ch 11, 13, 29). Current edition or most recent preceeding edition. 1 NEC © Current edition or most recent preceeding edition.', 'Quote re-checked word for word on the official page by the Academy source check.'),
  ('adoption', (md5('academykb:adoption:st:IL:irc:irc-under-the-illinois-residential-building-code-a')::uuid)::text, '2026-11-22T02:26:12Z'::timestamptz, 'official_text', 'verified', 'https://cdb.illinois.gov/business/codes/buildingcodesregulations.html', 'b893845507294f1554cd5d3c7899e063df67f5b4a71f852b7d5805d8aa537438', 'Residential buildings in jurisdictions that have not adopted a building code where NOT agreed to by the home purchaser and home builder. New construction: IRC © Current edition. (1/1/24 excluding IV and VII)', 'Quote re-checked word for word on the official page by the Academy source check.'),
  ('jurisdiction', 'IL', '2026-11-22T02:26:12Z'::timestamptz, 'official_text', 'verified', 'https://cdb.illinois.gov/business/codes/buildingcodesregulations.html', null, 'The State of Illinois recently passed legislation ( Public Act 103-0510 ) changing the Capital Development Board Act to require statewide building codes effective 1/1/2025. Until then, units of local government such as cities and counties can adopt codes of their choice.', 'Statewide code model, re-checked on the official page.'),
  ('adoption', (md5('academykb:adoption:st:IN:irc:2018')::uuid)::text, '2026-11-22T02:26:12Z'::timestamptz, 'official_text', 'verified', 'https://secure.iot.in.gov/dhs/files/Adoption-and-Implementation-of-2020-Indiana-Residential-Code.pdf', '5d00bfe618358211ec96592e317095dacc3e79e92ff4360091566b2de3bf7d7c', 'The 2020 Indiana Residential Code (675 IAC 14-4.4) went into effect on December 26, 2019. It applies to all construction on Class 2 structures and their accessory structures. The document consists of the International Code Council''s (ICC) model 2018 International Residential Code, as modified by Indiana state amendments.', 'Quote re-checked word for word on the official page by the Academy source check.'),
  ('adoption', (md5('academykb:adoption:st:IN:ibc:2012')::uuid)::text, '2026-11-22T02:26:12Z'::timestamptz, 'official_text', 'verified', 'https://www.in.gov/dhs/fire-and-building-safety/fpbsc-rules/', '491968d95c1640b3ba58deedd42f5e2f58470b16685af271b6592f32c793dc26', '675 IAC 13-2.6 2014 Indiana Building Code International Building Code, 2012 Edition, First Printing ANSI A117.1 Accessible and Usable Buildings and Facilities, 2009 Edition, First Printing Currently in Effect Effective: 12/1/2014', 'Quote re-checked word for word on the official page by the Academy source check.'),
  ('adoption', (md5('academykb:adoption:st:IN:ipc:2006')::uuid)::text, '2026-11-22T02:26:12Z'::timestamptz, 'official_text', 'verified', 'https://www.in.gov/dhs/fire-and-building-safety/fpbsc-rules/', '491968d95c1640b3ba58deedd42f5e2f58470b16685af271b6592f32c793dc26', '675 IAC 16-1.4 2012 Indiana Plumbing Code International Plumbing Code, 2006 Edition, Second Printing Currently in Effect Effective: 12/24/2012', 'Quote re-checked word for word on the official page by the Academy source check.'),
  ('adoption', (md5('academykb:adoption:st:IN:imc:2012')::uuid)::text, '2026-11-22T02:26:12Z'::timestamptz, 'official_text', 'verified', 'https://www.in.gov/dhs/fire-and-building-safety/fpbsc-rules/', '491968d95c1640b3ba58deedd42f5e2f58470b16685af271b6592f32c793dc26', '675 IAC 18-1.6 2014 Indiana Mechanical Code International Mechanical Code, 2012 Edition, First Printing Currently in Effect Effective: 12/1/2014', 'Quote re-checked word for word on the official page by the Academy source check.'),
  ('adoption', (md5('academykb:adoption:st:IN:ifgc:2012')::uuid)::text, '2026-11-22T02:26:12Z'::timestamptz, 'official_text', 'verified', 'https://www.in.gov/dhs/fire-and-building-safety/fpbsc-rules/', '491968d95c1640b3ba58deedd42f5e2f58470b16685af271b6592f32c793dc26', '675 IAC 25-3 2014 Indiana Fuel Gas Code International Fuel Gas Code, 2012 Edition, Second Printing Currently in Effect Effective: 12/1/2014', 'Quote re-checked word for word on the official page by the Academy source check.'),
  ('adoption', (md5('academykb:adoption:st:IN:ifc:2012')::uuid)::text, '2026-11-22T02:26:12Z'::timestamptz, 'official_text', 'verified', 'https://www.in.gov/dhs/fire-and-building-safety/fpbsc-rules/', '491968d95c1640b3ba58deedd42f5e2f58470b16685af271b6592f32c793dc26', '675 IAC 22-2.5 2014 Indiana Fire Code International Fire Code, 2012 Edition, First Printing Currently in Effect Effective: 12/1/2014', 'Quote re-checked word for word on the official page by the Academy source check.'),
  ('adoption', (md5('academykb:adoption:st:IN:ashrae_90_1:2007')::uuid)::text, '2026-11-22T02:26:12Z'::timestamptz, 'official_text', 'verified', 'https://www.in.gov/dhs/fire-and-building-safety/fpbsc-rules/', '491968d95c1640b3ba58deedd42f5e2f58470b16685af271b6592f32c793dc26', '675 IAC 19-4 2010 Indiana Energy Conservation Code ANSI/ASHRAE 90.1 Energy Standard for Buildings Except Low-Rise Residential Buildings, 2007 Edition, I-P Edition Currently in Effect Effective: 5/6/2010', 'Quote re-checked word for word on the official page by the Academy source check.'),
  ('jurisdiction', 'IN', '2026-11-22T02:26:12Z'::timestamptz, 'official_text', 'verified', 'https://secure.iot.in.gov/dhs/files/Adoption-and-Implementation-of-2020-Indiana-Residential-Code.pdf', null, 'Since that date, the 2020 Indiana Residential Code has been in full force and effect in every location within the state of Indiana. There are no jurisdictions or locations in the state in which the code is not in effect. Further, all local units of government are statutorily mandated to require compliance with the code, just as they are with all rules of the Fire Prevention and Building Safety Commission. See IC 36-7-2-9.', 'Statewide code model, re-checked on the official page.'),
  ('adoption', (md5('academykb:adoption:st:KS:ifc:2006')::uuid)::text, '2026-11-22T02:26:12Z'::timestamptz, 'official_text', 'verified', 'https://rules.ks.gov/api/policy-library-public/collections/0ae1e448-f5a1-4e09-9d6d-a488ac7c284a/policies/1ebc02f6-abe2-4127-9e00-a266d7216853/document/390df88f-493d-4a76-b770-67ec7299c0a3', 'bbce5f478cf885fa1ec4a0d621dfeef367470c0e0e371c52a25d9832f199ee04', '(b) international fire code (IFC), international code council, 2006 edition, including the appendices but excluding the following: (1) Chapters 22, 30, 33, 34, 35, 36, and 38;', 'Quote re-checked word for word on the official page by the Academy source check.'),
  ('adoption', (md5('academykb:adoption:st:KS:ibc:2006')::uuid)::text, '2026-11-22T02:26:12Z'::timestamptz, 'official_text', 'verified', 'https://rules.ks.gov/api/policy-library-public/collections/0ae1e448-f5a1-4e09-9d6d-a488ac7c284a/policies/1ebc02f6-abe2-4127-9e00-a266d7216853/document/390df88f-493d-4a76-b770-67ec7299c0a3', 'bbce5f478cf885fa1ec4a0d621dfeef367470c0e0e371c52a25d9832f199ee04', '(a) International building code (IBC), international code council, 2006 edition, including the appendices but excluding the references in chapter 35 to NFPA 13, 13D, 13R, 14, 30, 72, 101, and 110;', 'Quote re-checked word for word on the official page by the Academy source check.'),
  ('adoption', (md5('academykb:adoption:st:KS:nec:2008')::uuid)::text, '2026-11-22T02:26:12Z'::timestamptz, 'official_text', 'verified', 'https://rules.ks.gov/api/policy-library-public/collections/0ae1e448-f5a1-4e09-9d6d-a488ac7c284a/policies/1ebc02f6-abe2-4127-9e00-a266d7216853/document/390df88f-493d-4a76-b770-67ec7299c0a3', 'bbce5f478cf885fa1ec4a0d621dfeef367470c0e0e371c52a25d9832f199ee04', '(n) national electric code. NFPA standard no. 70, including annexes A, B, C, D, E, F, G, and H, 2008 edition;', 'Quote re-checked word for word on the official page by the Academy source check.'),
  ('jurisdiction', 'KS', '2026-11-22T02:26:12Z'::timestamptz, 'official_text', 'verified', 'https://ksrevisor.gov/statutes/chapters/ch12/012_030_0009.html', null, 'Any city is hereby authorized and empowered to incorporate in an ordinance by reference, in the manner hereinafter provided, any standard or model code or ordinance, regulation having the effect of law of a state officer, board or other agency, or statute, or portions thereof on any subject on which a city may legislate', 'Statewide code model, re-checked on the official page.'),
  ('adoption', (md5('academykb:adoption:st:KY:irc:2015')::uuid)::text, '2026-11-22T02:26:12Z'::timestamptz, 'official_text', 'verified', 'https://apps.legislature.ky.gov/law/kar/titles/815/007/125/', 'a22b6b0eac3ce26b39fd15dfb437bc29eb5fb1822fff04b3edae36cfe410672d', 'the 2015 International Residential Code for One (1) and Two (2) Family Dwellings (IRC) shall be the mandatory state residential building code for all single-family dwellings, two (2) family dwellings, and townhouses constructed in Kentucky, except that the Kentucky amendments in the 2018 Kentucky Residential Code shall supersede any conflicting provision in the 2015 IRC. ... 50 Ky.R. 1976; 51 Ky.R. 501; eff. 12-3-2024.)', 'Quote re-checked word for word on the official page by the Academy source check.'),
  ('adoption', (md5('academykb:adoption:st:KY:ibc:2015')::uuid)::text, '2026-11-22T02:26:12Z'::timestamptz, 'official_text', 'verified', 'https://apps.legislature.ky.gov/law/kar/titles/815/007/120/', '00f972994852ac54ee37e63b7fc11d098915d529ee125a683c57e05e87a64e81', 'The 2015 International Building shall be the mandatory state building code for all buildings constructed in Kentucky except that: (1) The Kentucky amendments in the 2018 Kentucky Building Code shall supersede any conflicting provision in the 2015 International Building Code; ... 50 Ky.R. 1973; 51 Ky.R. 500; eff. 12-3-2024.)', 'Quote re-checked word for word on the official page by the Academy source check.'),
  ('adoption', (md5('academykb:adoption:st:KY:imc:2015')::uuid)::text, '2026-11-22T02:26:12Z'::timestamptz, 'official_text', 'verified', 'https://dhbc.ky.gov/Documents/Find%20Currently%20Enforced%20Code.pdf', 'ab2f3968603afd02cc36a854db6f195b677897503656ddbe0909f9354bbce647', '2015 International Mechanical Code', 'Quote re-checked word for word on the official page by the Academy source check.'),
  ('adoption', (md5('academykb:adoption:st:KY:iebc:2015')::uuid)::text, '2026-11-22T02:26:12Z'::timestamptz, 'official_text', 'verified', 'https://dhbc.ky.gov/Documents/Find%20Currently%20Enforced%20Code.pdf', 'ab2f3968603afd02cc36a854db6f195b677897503656ddbe0909f9354bbce647', '2015 International Existing Building Code', 'Quote re-checked word for word on the official page by the Academy source check.'),
  ('adoption', (md5('academykb:adoption:st:KY:iecc:2012')::uuid)::text, '2026-11-22T02:26:12Z'::timestamptz, 'official_text', 'verified', 'https://dhbc.ky.gov/Documents/Find%20Currently%20Enforced%20Code.pdf', 'ab2f3968603afd02cc36a854db6f195b677897503656ddbe0909f9354bbce647', '2012 International Energy Conservation Code (for use with commercial buildings only)', 'Quote re-checked word for word on the official page by the Academy source check.'),
  ('adoption', (md5('academykb:adoption:st:KY:iecc:2009')::uuid)::text, '2026-11-22T02:26:12Z'::timestamptz, 'official_text', 'verified', 'https://dhbc.ky.gov/Documents/Find%20Currently%20Enforced%20Code.pdf', 'ab2f3968603afd02cc36a854db6f195b677897503656ddbe0909f9354bbce647', '2009 International Energy Conservation Code (for use with residential buildings only- see definition in IECC)', 'Quote re-checked word for word on the official page by the Academy source check.'),
  ('adoption', (md5('academykb:adoption:st:KY:nfpa54:2012')::uuid)::text, '2026-11-22T02:26:12Z'::timestamptz, 'official_text', 'verified', 'https://dhbc.ky.gov/Documents/Find%20Currently%20Enforced%20Code.pdf', 'ab2f3968603afd02cc36a854db6f195b677897503656ddbe0909f9354bbce647', '2012 NFPA 54 - National Fuel Gas Code', 'Quote re-checked word for word on the official page by the Academy source check.'),
  ('adoption', (md5('academykb:adoption:st:KY:nec:2023')::uuid)::text, '2026-11-22T02:26:12Z'::timestamptz, 'official_text', 'verified', 'https://dhbc.ky.gov/Documents/July%2015%202026%20NEC%20Update.pdf', '8d7af7063497b284fcbb20c04182912c88a24deefd0b62329c0f748596acc6e9', 'This is a reminder that effective July 15, 2026, several provisions of the 2023 National Electrical Code (NEC) that were delayed under the 2018 Kentucky Residential Code will become fully enforceable.', 'Quote re-checked word for word on the official page by the Academy source check.'),
  ('adoption', (md5('academykb:adoption:st:KY:nfpa1:2018')::uuid)::text, '2026-11-22T02:26:12Z'::timestamptz, 'official_text', 'verified', 'https://apps.legislature.ky.gov/law/kar/titles/815/010/060/', 'af290331f42342c1dc9214ddc4466c873c625c1b0f27f8f0c6d3199fb35bbe6d', 'NFPA 1, Uniform Fire Code, 2018 edition, and the NFPA referenced standards included in Chapter 2 of NFPA 1 except: ... 49 Ky.R. 2145; 50 Ky.R. 673; eff 9-26-2023.)', 'Quote re-checked word for word on the official page by the Academy source check.'),
  ('adoption', (md5('academykb:adoption:st:KY:state_plumbing:kentucky-state-plumbing-law-regulations-code')::uuid)::text, '2026-11-22T02:26:12Z'::timestamptz, 'official_text', 'verified', 'https://dhbc.ky.gov/Documents/Find%20Currently%20Enforced%20Code.pdf', 'ab2f3968603afd02cc36a854db6f195b677897503656ddbe0909f9354bbce647', 'Kentucky State Plumbing Law, Regulations & Code (815 KAR Chapter 20)', 'Quote re-checked word for word on the official page by the Academy source check.'),
  ('jurisdiction', 'KY', '2026-11-22T02:26:12Z'::timestamptz, 'official_text', 'verified', 'https://apps.legislature.ky.gov/law/statutes/statute.aspx?id=52659', null, 'Each local government shall employ a building official or inspector and other code enforcement personnel as necessary, or shall contract for inspection and code enforcement services in accordance with subsections (8) and (11) of this section to enforce the Uniform State Building Code within the boundaries of its jurisdiction, except that permits, inspections, and certificates of occupancy shall not be mandatory for single-family residences unless a local government passes an ordinance requiring inspections of single-family residences.', 'Statewide code model, re-checked on the official page.'),
