  ('adoption', (md5('academykb:adoption:st:LA:ipc:2021')::uuid)::text, '2026-11-22T02:26:12Z'::timestamptz, 'official_text', 'verified', 'https://luccc.louisiana.gov/wp-content/uploads/2025/11/LSUCCC_Louisiana-Construction-Code-Information.pdf', '0d9a643c668bc8c6387fcf9df7e5513567af99b7ba26216b71abf3450562a553', 'International Plumbing Code (IPC) 2021 ... 2021 ICC Codes January 1, 2023', 'Quote re-checked word for word on the official page by the Academy source check.'),
  ('adoption', (md5('academykb:adoption:st:LA:iecc:2021')::uuid)::text, '2026-11-22T02:26:12Z'::timestamptz, 'official_text', 'verified', 'https://luccc.louisiana.gov/wp-content/uploads/2025/11/LSUCCC_Louisiana-Construction-Code-Information.pdf', '0d9a643c668bc8c6387fcf9df7e5513567af99b7ba26216b71abf3450562a553', 'International Energy Conservation Code (IECC) 2021 ... 2021 IECC July 1, 2023 ... On 07/01/2023, the International Energy Conservation Code (IECC) became effective.', 'Quote re-checked word for word on the official page by the Academy source check.'),
  ('adoption', (md5('academykb:adoption:st:LA:nec:2020')::uuid)::text, '2026-11-22T02:26:12Z'::timestamptz, 'official_text', 'verified', 'https://luccc.louisiana.gov/wp-content/uploads/2025/11/LSUCCC_Louisiana-Construction-Code-Information.pdf', '0d9a643c668bc8c6387fcf9df7e5513567af99b7ba26216b71abf3450562a553', 'National Electrical Code (NEC) 2020 ... 2020 NEC January 1, 2023', 'Quote re-checked word for word on the official page by the Academy source check.'),
  ('jurisdiction', 'LA', '2026-11-22T02:26:12Z'::timestamptz, 'official_text', 'verified', 'https://legis.la.gov/Legis/LawPrint.aspx?d=97797', null, 'Notwithstanding any other law to the contrary relating to the authority of local governments to enforce construction codes, all municipalities and parishes in this state shall enforce only the construction codes provided for in this Part.', 'Statewide code model, re-checked on the official page.'),
  ('adoption', (md5('academykb:adoption:st:MA:ibc:2021')::uuid)::text, '2026-11-22T02:26:12Z'::timestamptz, 'official_text', 'verified', 'https://www.sec.state.ma.us/reg_pub/pdf/700/780001.pdf', 'a61e48e7ab7131e9ffd88c200560ea1c860bd1f30cd227ef1b70bad5bd5f560c', '101.1 Adoption and Title. The Board of Building Regulations and Standards ("BBRS") adopts and incorporates by reference, the International Building Code-2021 ("IBC"), as periodically amended by errata, the following chapters, as well as 110.R1 through 110.R7 and Appendices A through O. These, together with modifications as set forth, shall collectively comprise 780 CMR, otherwise known as the Massachusetts State Building Code, Tenth Edition, Base Volume.', 'Quote re-checked word for word on the official page by the Academy source check.'),
  ('adoption', (md5('academykb:adoption:st:MA:irc:2021')::uuid)::text, '2026-11-22T02:26:12Z'::timestamptz, 'official_text', 'verified', 'https://www.sec.state.ma.us/reg_pub/pdf/700/780051.pdf', '08f2573185de4d92c35490e61fe2b695254e17b5ec49345e0f1d2e1386d9a8ba', 'R101.1 Adoption and Title. The Board of Building Regulations and Standards ("BBRS") adopts and incorporates by reference the International Residential Code, 2021 ("IBC"), as periodically amended by errata, the following chapters, as well as 110.R1 through 115AA. These, together with modifications as set forth, shall collectively comprise 780 CMR 51.00: Massachusetts Residential Code, otherwise known as the Massachusetts State Building Code, Tenth Edition, Residential Volume.', 'Quote re-checked word for word on the official page by the Academy source check.'),
  ('adoption', (md5('academykb:adoption:st:MA:iebc:2021')::uuid)::text, '2026-11-22T02:26:12Z'::timestamptz, 'official_text', 'verified', 'https://www.sec.state.ma.us/reg_pub/pdf/700/780001.pdf', 'a61e48e7ab7131e9ffd88c200560ea1c860bd1f30cd227ef1b70bad5bd5f560c', '101.4.16 Existing Buildings. See 780 CMR 34.00: Existing Building Code and the provisions of the 2021 International Existing Building Code as amended. 780 CMR 34.00 shall apply to matters governing the repair, alteration, change of occupancy, addition to and relocation of existing buildings.', 'Quote re-checked word for word on the official page by the Academy source check.'),
  ('adoption', (md5('academykb:adoption:st:MA:imc:2021')::uuid)::text, '2026-11-22T02:26:12Z'::timestamptz, 'official_text', 'verified', 'https://www.sec.state.ma.us/reg_pub/pdf/700/780001.pdf', 'a61e48e7ab7131e9ffd88c200560ea1c860bd1f30cd227ef1b70bad5bd5f560c', '101.4.2 Mechanical. The installation of mechanical systems shall generally be governed by the International Mechanical Code - 2021 ("IMC").', 'Quote re-checked word for word on the official page by the Academy source check.'),
  ('adoption', (md5('academykb:adoption:st:MA:iecc:2021')::uuid)::text, '2026-11-22T02:26:12Z'::timestamptz, 'official_text', 'verified', 'https://www.sec.state.ma.us/reg_pub/pdf/700/780051.pdf', '08f2573185de4d92c35490e61fe2b695254e17b5ec49345e0f1d2e1386d9a8ba', '[E] 1101.1.1 Criteria. Buildings shall be designed and constructed in accordance with the 2021 International Energy Conservation Code (IECC) with Massachusetts Amendments contained herein.', 'Quote re-checked word for word on the official page by the Academy source check.'),
  ('adoption', (md5('academykb:adoption:st:MA:nec:2026')::uuid)::text, '2026-11-22T02:26:12Z'::timestamptz, 'official_text', 'verified', 'https://www.sec.state.ma.us/reg_pub/pdf/500/527012.pdf', 'c9ee3e367bb7833ee9cf6513b8395f3ab4f5cbe009f5e161ac3cb0e3dd5d7d80', 'The Massachusetts Electrical Code (527 CMR 12.00) of the Board of Fire Prevention Regulations (BFPR) shall be the 2026 National Electrical Code (NEC), as published by the National Fire Protection Association (NFPA) as NFPA 70 in the form released by vote of the NFPA Standards Council on August 20, 2025', 'Quote re-checked word for word on the official page by the Academy source check.'),
  ('adoption', (md5('academykb:adoption:st:MA:nfpa1:2021')::uuid)::text, '2026-11-22T02:26:12Z'::timestamptz, 'official_text', 'verified', 'https://www.sec.state.ma.us/reg_pub/pdf/500/527001.pdf', '9c00b8391c3c47573f3f765879fccfc1829109e4ba17a0e5b96a35c8a2ed07c5', '527 CMR 1.00 adopts and incorporates, the provisions of (National Fire Protection Association) NFPA 1 Fire Code - 2021 edition as modified by 1.05.', 'Quote re-checked word for word on the official page by the Academy source check.'),
  ('jurisdiction', 'MA', '2026-11-22T02:26:12Z'::timestamptz, 'official_text', 'verified', 'https://www.sec.state.ma.us/reg_pub/pdf/700/780001.pdf', null, '101.2 Scope. 780 CMR shall be the building code for all towns, cities, state agencies or authorities in accordance with M.G.L. c. 143, §§ 93 through 100.', 'Statewide code model, re-checked on the official page.'),
  ('adoption', (md5('academykb:adoption:st:MD:ibc:2021')::uuid)::text, '2026-11-22T02:26:12Z'::timestamptz, 'official_text', 'verified', 'https://labor.maryland.gov/labor/build/buildadmin.shtml', '5c455117ffe73efa3d4e28487e622913605b35341f81fa3825548fa834f344d8', 'State (the Department) has adopted the 2021 edition of IBC, IRC, & IECC, with state amendments, for COMAR 09.12.50 Model Performance Code & COMAR 09.12.51 Maryland. The effective date is May 29, 2023. State law requires local jurisdiction to start implementing & enforcing the new requirements by May 29, 2024.', 'Quote re-checked word for word on the official page by the Academy source check.'),
  ('adoption', (md5('academykb:adoption:st:MD:irc:2021')::uuid)::text, '2026-11-22T02:26:12Z'::timestamptz, 'official_text', 'verified', 'https://labor.maryland.gov/labor/build/buildadmin.shtml', '5c455117ffe73efa3d4e28487e622913605b35341f81fa3825548fa834f344d8', 'State (the Department) has adopted the 2021 edition of IBC, IRC, & IECC, with state amendments, for COMAR 09.12.50 Model Performance Code & COMAR 09.12.51 Maryland. The effective date is May 29, 2023. State law requires local jurisdiction to start implementing & enforcing the new requirements by May 29, 2024.', 'Quote re-checked word for word on the official page by the Academy source check.'),
  ('adoption', (md5('academykb:adoption:st:MD:iecc:2021')::uuid)::text, '2026-11-22T02:26:12Z'::timestamptz, 'official_text', 'verified', 'https://labor.maryland.gov/labor/build/buildadmin.shtml', '5c455117ffe73efa3d4e28487e622913605b35341f81fa3825548fa834f344d8', 'State (the Department) has adopted the 2021 edition of IBC, IRC, & IECC, with state amendments, for COMAR 09.12.50 Model Performance Code & COMAR 09.12.51 Maryland. The effective date is May 29, 2023. State law requires local jurisdiction to start implementing & enforcing the new requirements by May 29, 2024.', 'Quote re-checked word for word on the official page by the Academy source check.'),
  ('adoption', (md5('academykb:adoption:st:MD:nfpa1:2024')::uuid)::text, '2026-11-22T02:26:12Z'::timestamptz, 'official_text', 'verified', 'https://mdsp.maryland.gov/firemarshal/Documents/State%20Fire%20Prevention%20Code%202024%20Adopted%20Errata%20.pdf', '42a6d35d1479750ccf1b30f61240ae6a659bdb5df9353546c96f3882df88290b', 'Authority: Public Safety Article §6-206 and 6-501 (Amended effective June 23, 2025) (Errata #1 issued July 15, 2025) .01 Title. This chapter shall be known and may be cited as the State Fire Prevention Code. ... B. This chapter incorporates by reference NFPA 1 Fire Code (2024 Edition), except as amended in Regulations .08 and .09 of this chapter, and NFPA 101 Life Safety Code (2024 Edition)', 'Quote re-checked word for word on the official page by the Academy source check.'),
  ('jurisdiction', 'MD', '2026-11-22T02:26:12Z'::timestamptz, 'official_text', 'verified', 'https://mgaleg.maryland.gov/mgawebsite/Laws/StatuteText?article=gps&section=12-504&enactments=false', null, '(1) A local jurisdiction may adopt local amendments to the Standards if the local amendments do not: (i) prohibit the minimum implementation and enforcement activities set forth in § 12–505 of this subtitle; (ii) weaken energy conservation and efficiency provisions contained in the Standards;', 'Statewide code model, re-checked on the official page.'),
  ('adoption', (md5('academykb:adoption:st:ME:ibc:2021')::uuid)::text, '2026-11-22T02:26:12Z'::timestamptz, 'official_text', 'verified', 'https://www.maine.gov/dps/fmo/sites/maine.gov.dps.fmo/files/inline-files/642C003.pdf', '714acf6cd2d7825c1a9ee9e9f0246dfb4f4ff129a69211a004e041ad521b834e', '1. IBC. “IBC” means the 2021 International Building Code, published by the International Code Council, Inc.', 'Quote re-checked word for word on the official page by the Academy source check.'),
