  ('adoption', (md5('academykb:adoption:st:OK:ifgc:2024')::uuid)::text, '2026-11-22T02:26:12Z'::timestamptz, 'official_text', 'verified', 'https://oklahoma.gov/content/dam/ok/en/oubcc/documents/rules/2026%2009%2014%20IFGC%202024%20Permanent%20Rule.pdf', '3755429fc6457dc3e9b172cd3a2c932d5696d2ac64c81308e846d8c6a64ba8ae', 'the OUBCC is adopting the first printing of the 2024 Edition of the International Fuel Gas Code® (IFGC®, 2024), effective September 14, 2026, as the permanent rule pursuant to Oklahoma law at OAC 748:20-12-1.', 'Quote re-checked word for word on the official page by the Academy source check.'),
  ('adoption', (md5('academykb:adoption:st:OK:imc:2024')::uuid)::text, '2026-11-22T02:26:12Z'::timestamptz, 'official_text', 'verified', 'https://oklahoma.gov/content/dam/ok/en/oubcc/documents/rules/2026%2009%2014%20IMC%20Permanent%20Rule.pdf', 'fd0c6f78a22770572b6573d59e69e172af5204574a455da7cc155501e79fe802', 'the OUBCC is adopting the first printing of the 2024 Edition of the International Mechanical Code® (IMC®, 2024), effective September 14, 2026, as the permanent rule pursuant to Oklahoma law at OAC 748:20-14-1.', 'Quote re-checked word for word on the official page by the Academy source check.'),
  ('adoption', (md5('academykb:adoption:st:OK:ipc:2024')::uuid)::text, '2026-11-22T02:26:12Z'::timestamptz, 'official_text', 'verified', 'https://oklahoma.gov/content/dam/ok/en/oubcc/documents/rules/2026%2009%2014%20IPC%202026%20Permanent%20Rule%20.pdf', 'c3175b15b755552604b75c3d3f648127434fb08ba62f84b44e85d114694a2d8d', 'the OUBCC is adopting the first printing of the 2024 Edition of the International Plumbing Code® (IPC®, 2024), effective September 14, 2026, as the permanent rule pursuant to Oklahoma law at OAC 748:20-16-1.', 'Quote re-checked word for word on the official page by the Academy source check.'),
  ('adoption', (md5('academykb:adoption:st:OK:nec:2023')::uuid)::text, '2026-11-22T02:26:12Z'::timestamptz, 'official_text', 'verified', 'https://oklahoma.gov/content/dam/ok/en/oubcc/documents/rules/2022%2009%2014%20NEC%202023%20Permanent%20Rule.pdf', '3b19e45a4e5b57d1da7d2a4d5d8da194c6d8c4a046f43969f006e54d52ba286e', '[Source: Amended at 41 Ok Reg, Number 21, effective 9-14-24] 748:20-10-1. Adoption of the National Electrical Code®, 2023 Edition (NEC® 2023) (a) The Oklahoma Uniform Building Code Commission (the "OUBCC") hereby adopts the National Electrical Code®, 2023 Edition - NFPA 70® (NEC® 2023), as amended and modified in this subchapter as the statewide minimum code', 'Quote re-checked word for word on the official page by the Academy source check.'),
  ('jurisdiction', 'OK', '2026-11-22T02:26:12Z'::timestamptz, 'official_text', 'verified', 'https://oklahoma.gov/content/dam/ok/en/oubcc/documents/statute-and-updated-versions/OUBCC%20Unofficial%20Copy%20of%20State%20Statutes%20-%20Title%2059%20Sections%201000.20%20through%201000.31.pdf', null, 'A. The Oklahoma Uniform Building Code Commission shall have the power and the duty to review and adopt all codes and standards for residential and commercial construction to be used by all entities within this state. Codes and standards adopted by the Commission shall be the minimum standards for residential and commercial construction in this state.', 'Statewide code model, re-checked on the official page.'),
  ('adoption', (md5('academykb:adoption:st:OR:ibc:2024')::uuid)::text, '2026-11-22T02:26:12Z'::timestamptz, 'official_text', 'verified', 'https://secure.sos.state.or.us/oard/displayDivisionRules.action?selectedDivision=4170', '433df166de8e35ad1b3993b94d29e8b5d0340d8b674e92c435c15dda65e449df', '(2) Effective October 1, 2025, the 2025 Oregon Structural Specialty Code is: (a) The 2024 Edition of the International Building Code, 2024 International Fire Code (IFC) new construction provisions, 2024 International Existing Building Code (IEBC), as published by the International Code Council, and amended by the Building Codes Division;', 'Quote re-checked word for word on the official page by the Academy source check.'),
  ('adoption', (md5('academykb:adoption:st:OR:iebc:2024')::uuid)::text, '2026-11-22T02:26:12Z'::timestamptz, 'official_text', 'verified', 'https://secure.sos.state.or.us/oard/displayDivisionRules.action?selectedDivision=4170', '433df166de8e35ad1b3993b94d29e8b5d0340d8b674e92c435c15dda65e449df', '(2) Effective October 1, 2025, the 2025 Oregon Structural Specialty Code is: (a) The 2024 Edition of the International Building Code, 2024 International Fire Code (IFC) new construction provisions, 2024 International Existing Building Code (IEBC), as published by the International Code Council, and amended by the Building Codes Division;', 'Quote re-checked word for word on the official page by the Academy source check.'),
  ('adoption', (md5('academykb:adoption:st:OR:irc:2024')::uuid)::text, '2026-11-22T02:26:12Z'::timestamptz, 'official_text', 'verified', 'https://secure.sos.state.or.us/oard/displayDivisionRules.action?selectedDivision=4173', '87ab21464bf6f1af8079a3223b6012fb4533d5e6f9e09d61391e4df1c21f05aa', '(3) Effective October 1, 2026, the 2026 Oregon Residential Specialty Code consists of the following: (a) The 2024 edition of the International Residential Code for One- and Two-Family Dwellings as published by the International Code Council, Inc., Chapters 1 through 24 and Chapter 44,', 'Quote re-checked word for word on the official page by the Academy source check.'),
  ('adoption', (md5('academykb:adoption:st:OR:imc:2024')::uuid)::text, '2026-11-22T02:26:12Z'::timestamptz, 'official_text', 'verified', 'https://secure.sos.state.or.us/oard/displayDivisionRules.action?selectedDivision=4168', '39dcb78e5bdcdf0438f83afd0a79f2d46f76432334f9f85a27fefe43d7369a66', '(2) Effective October 1, 2025, the 2025 Oregon Mechanical Specialty Code is the 2024 Editions of the International Mechanical Code and International Fuel Gas Code as published by the International Code Council and amended by the Building Codes Division.', 'Quote re-checked word for word on the official page by the Academy source check.'),
  ('adoption', (md5('academykb:adoption:st:OR:ifgc:2024')::uuid)::text, '2026-11-22T02:26:12Z'::timestamptz, 'official_text', 'verified', 'https://secure.sos.state.or.us/oard/displayDivisionRules.action?selectedDivision=4168', '39dcb78e5bdcdf0438f83afd0a79f2d46f76432334f9f85a27fefe43d7369a66', '(2) Effective October 1, 2025, the 2025 Oregon Mechanical Specialty Code is the 2024 Editions of the International Mechanical Code and International Fuel Gas Code as published by the International Code Council and amended by the Building Codes Division.', 'Quote re-checked word for word on the official page by the Academy source check.'),
  ('adoption', (md5('academykb:adoption:st:OR:upc:2024')::uuid)::text, '2026-11-22T02:26:12Z'::timestamptz, 'official_text', 'verified', 'https://secure.sos.state.or.us/oard/displayDivisionRules.action?selectedDivision=4190', 'f1cc244048fec5cdf5f43fec475095ea5adef9ea6e259ffd6d577027b4ec3144', '(2) Effective October 1, 2026, the 2026 Oregon Plumbing Specialty Code is based upon the following: (a) The 2024 edition of the Uniform Plumbing Code, Fifth Printing; (b) Chapters 1–11 and 13–17; (c) Appendices A, B, C, D, E, K, and M; and (d) As further amended by the division.', 'Quote re-checked word for word on the official page by the Academy source check.'),
  ('adoption', (md5('academykb:adoption:st:OR:ifc:2024')::uuid)::text, '2026-11-22T02:26:12Z'::timestamptz, 'official_text', 'verified', 'https://secure.sos.state.or.us/oard/displayDivisionRules.action?selectedDivision=3805', 'dcd9a5c29282804558a9cf2dcad11eda5320788bddba050c5608a5d964914cfe', '(2) Effective October 1, 2025, the 2025 Oregon Fire Code which is the 2024 edition of the International Fire Code, as published by the International Code Council, and as amended by the Department of the State Fire Marshal , is adopted.', 'Quote re-checked word for word on the official page by the Academy source check.'),
  ('adoption', (md5('academykb:adoption:st:OR:ashrae_90_1:2022')::uuid)::text, '2026-11-22T02:26:12Z'::timestamptz, 'official_text', 'verified', 'https://secure.sos.state.or.us/oard/displayDivisionRules.action?selectedDivision=4170', '433df166de8e35ad1b3993b94d29e8b5d0340d8b674e92c435c15dda65e449df', '(2) Effective January 1, 2025, the Oregon Energy Efficiency Specialty Code shall consist of ANSI/ASHRAE/IES Standard 90.1-2022 with additional Oregon amendments as published by the Building Codes Division and available on the Division’s website, and shall be known as the 2025 Oregon Energy Efficiency Specialty Code.', 'Quote re-checked word for word on the official page by the Academy source check.'),
  ('adoption', (md5('academykb:adoption:st:OR:nec:2026')::uuid)::text, '2026-11-22T02:26:12Z'::timestamptz, 'official_text', 'verified', 'https://secure.sos.state.or.us/oard/displayDivisionRules.action?selectedDivision=4158', '2c22e8b27a5de3353c151284cf81972b2a8b1c3972e88cf2b8e8a6a67079cf7c', '(2) Effective October 1, 2026, the 2026 Oregon Electrical Specialty Code consists of the following: (a) 2026 edition of the NFPA 70, National Electrical Code (NEC), and as further amended by the division in OAR 918-305-0105 Table 1-E;', 'Quote re-checked word for word on the official page by the Academy source check.'),
  ('jurisdiction', 'OR', '2026-11-22T02:26:12Z'::timestamptz, 'official_text', 'verified', 'https://www.oregonlegislature.gov/bills_laws/ors/ors455.html', null, '(1) The state building code shall be applicable and uniform throughout this state and in all municipalities, and no municipality shall enact or enforce any ordinance, rule or regulation relating to the same matters encompassed by the state building code but which provides different requirements unless authorized by the Director of the Department of Consumer and Business Services.', 'Statewide code model, re-checked on the official page.'),
  ('adoption', (md5('academykb:adoption:st:PA:ibc:2021')::uuid)::text, '2026-11-22T02:26:12Z'::timestamptz, 'official_text', 'verified', 'https://www.pacodeandbulletin.gov/Display/pacode?file=/secure/pacode/data/034/chapter403/s403.21.html', '17e91038d258d999325810d98dc504e3a0c11fb6fb14c8e529e29cbfe9a3647a', '(a) The Department adopts and incorporates by reference the following codes as the Uniform Construction Code: (1) The provisions of Chapters 2—10, 12—29 and 31—35 of the ‘‘International Building Code of 2021,’’', 'Quote re-checked word for word on the official page by the Academy source check.'),
  ('adoption', (md5('academykb:adoption:st:PA:irc:2021')::uuid)::text, '2026-11-22T02:26:12Z'::timestamptz, 'official_text', 'verified', 'https://www.pacodeandbulletin.gov/Display/pacode?file=/secure/pacode/data/034/chapter403/s403.21.html', '17e91038d258d999325810d98dc504e3a0c11fb6fb14c8e529e29cbfe9a3647a', '(7) The ‘‘International Residential Code of 2021,’’ except that: (i) The provisions of R314.4 requiring interconnected smoke alarms do not apply to one-family and two-family dwellings undergoing alterations, repairs or additions.', 'Quote re-checked word for word on the official page by the Academy source check.'),
  ('adoption', (md5('academykb:adoption:st:PA:ipc:2021')::uuid)::text, '2026-11-22T02:26:12Z'::timestamptz, 'official_text', 'verified', 'https://www.pacodeandbulletin.gov/Display/pacode?file=/secure/pacode/data/034/chapter403/s403.21.html', '17e91038d258d999325810d98dc504e3a0c11fb6fb14c8e529e29cbfe9a3647a', '(6) The ‘‘International Plumbing Code of 2021’’ except: (i) A municipality within a county of the second class may not administer and enforce the ‘‘International Plumbing Code’’ adopted under this chapter.', 'Quote re-checked word for word on the official page by the Academy source check.'),
  ('adoption', (md5('academykb:adoption:st:PA:imc:2021')::uuid)::text, '2026-11-22T02:26:12Z'::timestamptz, 'official_text', 'verified', 'https://www.pacodeandbulletin.gov/Display/pacode?file=/secure/pacode/data/034/chapter403/s403.21.html', '17e91038d258d999325810d98dc504e3a0c11fb6fb14c8e529e29cbfe9a3647a', '(3) The ‘‘International Mechanical Code of 2021.’’ (4) The ‘‘International Fuel Gas Code of 2021.’’', 'Quote re-checked word for word on the official page by the Academy source check.'),
  ('adoption', (md5('academykb:adoption:st:PA:ifgc:2021')::uuid)::text, '2026-11-22T02:26:12Z'::timestamptz, 'official_text', 'verified', 'https://www.pacodeandbulletin.gov/Display/pacode?file=/secure/pacode/data/034/chapter403/s403.21.html', '17e91038d258d999325810d98dc504e3a0c11fb6fb14c8e529e29cbfe9a3647a', '(3) The ‘‘International Mechanical Code of 2021.’’ (4) The ‘‘International Fuel Gas Code of 2021.’’', 'Quote re-checked word for word on the official page by the Academy source check.'),
  ('adoption', (md5('academykb:adoption:st:PA:ifc:2021')::uuid)::text, '2026-11-22T02:26:12Z'::timestamptz, 'official_text', 'verified', 'https://www.pacodeandbulletin.gov/Display/pacode?file=/secure/pacode/data/034/chapter403/s403.21.html', '17e91038d258d999325810d98dc504e3a0c11fb6fb14c8e529e29cbfe9a3647a', '(8) The ‘‘International Fire Code of 2021’’ only to the extent it is referenced by other ICC codes adopted in this chapter.', 'Quote re-checked word for word on the official page by the Academy source check.'),
  ('adoption', (md5('academykb:adoption:st:PA:iecc:2021')::uuid)::text, '2026-11-22T02:26:12Z'::timestamptz, 'official_text', 'verified', 'https://www.pacodeandbulletin.gov/Display/pacode?file=/secure/pacode/data/034/chapter403/s403.21.html', '17e91038d258d999325810d98dc504e3a0c11fb6fb14c8e529e29cbfe9a3647a', '(9) The ‘‘International Energy Conservation Code of 2021’’ is adopted as follows: (i) {Reserved}.', 'Quote re-checked word for word on the official page by the Academy source check.'),
  ('adoption', (md5('academykb:adoption:st:PA:iebc:2021')::uuid)::text, '2026-11-22T02:26:12Z'::timestamptz, 'official_text', 'verified', 'https://www.pacodeandbulletin.gov/Display/pacode?file=/secure/pacode/data/034/chapter403/s403.21.html', '17e91038d258d999325810d98dc504e3a0c11fb6fb14c8e529e29cbfe9a3647a', '(10) The ‘‘International Existing Building Code of 2021’’ except: (i) The accessibility provisions contained in the following sections of the ‘‘International Existing Building Code of 2021’’ are excluded:', 'Quote re-checked word for word on the official page by the Academy source check.'),
  ('jurisdiction', 'PA', '2026-11-22T02:26:12Z'::timestamptz, 'official_text', 'verified', 'https://www.pa.gov/agencies/dli/programs-services/labor-management-relations/bureau-of-occupational-and-industrial-safety/uniform-construction-code-home', null, 'If a municipality has "OPTED-OUT," the Department is responsible for all commercial code enforcement in that municipality. The Department also has sole jurisdiction for all elevators and all state-owned buildings, no matter where they are located. Certified third party agencies hired by property owners (or their contractors) enforce the residential requirements of the UCC in all opt-out municipalities.', 'Statewide code model, re-checked on the official page.'),
  ('adoption', (md5('academykb:adoption:st:RI:ibc:2021')::uuid)::text, '2026-11-22T02:26:12Z'::timestamptz, 'official_text', 'verified', 'https://rules.sos.ri.gov/regulations/Part/510-00-00-1', '59d9825c029d9f16f6563d703bb5abfebe3544b857e20d49be8255a802137430', '1.2 Incorporated Materials A. The Building Code Standards Committee hereby adopts and incorporates as the Rhode Island Building Code the provisions of the International Building Code (IBC), 2021 edition, as published by the International Code Council, Inc. (ICC) not including any further editions or amendments thereof and only to the extent that the provisions therein are not inconsistent with R.I. Gen. Laws Chapter', 'Quote re-checked word for word on the official page by the Academy source check.'),
  ('adoption', (md5('academykb:adoption:st:RI:irc:2021')::uuid)::text, '2026-11-22T02:26:12Z'::timestamptz, 'official_text', 'verified', 'https://rules.sos.ri.gov/regulations/Part/510-00-00-2', 'f3ebe0d83ee6a5afd81bd1fe9eb0da95f29d49520b5bd92f32b148d5c0e22d3c', '2.2 Incorporated Materials A. The Building Code Standards Committee hereby adopts and incorporates as the Rhode Island One & Two-Family Dwelling Code the provisions of the International Residential Code (IRC), 2021 edition, as published by the International Code Council, Inc. (ICC) not including any further editions or amendments thereof and only to the extent that the provisions therein are not inconsistent with', 'Quote re-checked word for word on the official page by the Academy source check.'),
  ('adoption', (md5('academykb:adoption:st:RI:ipc:2021')::uuid)::text, '2026-11-22T02:26:12Z'::timestamptz, 'official_text', 'verified', 'https://rules.sos.ri.gov/regulations/Part/510-00-00-3', '28dee48c54a76a55b03294e18a5f3502a658eac156015c147fe90c2374c80a9c', '3.2 Incorporated Materials A. The Building Code Standards Committee hereby adopts and incorporates as the Rhode Island Plumbing Code the provisions of the International Plumbing Code (IPC), 2021 edition, as published by the International Code Council, Inc. (ICC) not including any further editions or amendments thereof and only to the extent that the provisions therein are not inconsistent with R.I. Gen. Laws Chapter', 'Quote re-checked word for word on the official page by the Academy source check.'),
  ('adoption', (md5('academykb:adoption:st:RI:imc:2021')::uuid)::text, '2026-11-22T02:26:12Z'::timestamptz, 'official_text', 'verified', 'https://rules.sos.ri.gov/regulations/Part/510-00-00-4', 'f08217e7e7bb451c2a012dfab248b5d806df47918a757ee4a8191330f1694ca6', '4.2 Incorporated Materials A. The Building Code Standards Committee hereby adopts and incorporates as the Rhode Island Mechanical Code the provisions of the International Mechanical Code (IMC), 2021 edition, as published by the International Code Council, Inc. (ICC) not including any further editions or amendments thereof and only to the extent that the provisions therein are not inconsistent with R.I. Gen. Laws', 'Quote re-checked word for word on the official page by the Academy source check.'),
  ('adoption', (md5('academykb:adoption:st:RI:nec:2023')::uuid)::text, '2026-11-22T02:26:12Z'::timestamptz, 'official_text', 'verified', 'https://rules.sos.ri.gov/regulations/Part/510-00-00-5', 'e99777b375ac8b80e844de43142f32f6460e780291d838ad705764dd75d6efaf', '5.2 Incorporated Materials A. The Building Code Standards Committee hereby adopts and incorporates as the Rhode Island Electrical Code the provisions of the National Electrical Code (NEC) 2023 edition, as published by the National Fire Protection Association (NFPA) not including any further editions or amendments thereof and only to the extent that the provisions therein are not inconsistent with R.I. Gen. Laws', 'Quote re-checked word for word on the official page by the Academy source check.'),
  ('adoption', (md5('academykb:adoption:st:RI:iebc:2021')::uuid)::text, '2026-11-22T02:26:12Z'::timestamptz, 'official_text', 'verified', 'https://rules.sos.ri.gov/regulations/Part/510-00-00-7', 'bc02deea1e08ba008c20b2fe80f9d8a1d2aa6a1dca7124f0002e765f913b4cf8', '7.2 Incorporated Materials A. The Building Code Standards Committee hereby adopts and incorporates as the Rhode Island Existing Building Code the provisions of the International Existing Building Code (IEBC), 2021 edition, as published by the International Code Council, Inc. (ICC) not including any further editions or amendments thereof and only to the extent that the provisions therein are not inconsistent with', 'Quote re-checked word for word on the official page by the Academy source check.'),
  ('adoption', (md5('academykb:adoption:st:RI:iecc:2024')::uuid)::text, '2026-11-22T02:26:12Z'::timestamptz, 'official_text', 'verified', 'https://rules.sos.ri.gov/regulations/Part/510-00-00-8', 'dc5549e51afced6635c489109009c1d9627b5dae30263b5851232479976d6a50', '8.2 Incorporated Materials A. The Building Code Standards Committee hereby adopts and incorporates as the Rhode Island Energy Conservation Code the provisions of the International Energy Conservation Code (IECC), 2024 edition, as published by the International Code Council, Inc. (ICC) not including any further editions or amendments thereof and only to the extent that the provisions therein are not inconsistent with', 'Quote re-checked word for word on the official page by the Academy source check.'),
  ('adoption', (md5('academykb:adoption:st:RI:ifgc:2021')::uuid)::text, '2026-11-22T02:26:12Z'::timestamptz, 'official_text', 'verified', 'https://rules.sos.ri.gov/regulations/Part/510-00-00-19', '583c25dbaa602d45049d5f43fe6d95c4efa09cd6ce372060adb4a395ff2255e7', '19.2 Incorporated Materials A. The Building Code Standards Committee hereby adopts and incorporates as the Rhode Island Fuel Gas Code the provisions of the International Fuel Gas Code (IFGC), 2021 edition, as published by the International Code Council, Inc. (ICC) not including any further editions or amendments thereof and only to the extent that the provisions therein are not inconsistent with R.I. Gen. Laws', 'Quote re-checked word for word on the official page by the Academy source check.'),
  ('adoption', (md5('academykb:adoption:st:RI:nfpa1:2021')::uuid)::text, '2026-11-22T02:26:12Z'::timestamptz, 'official_text', 'verified', 'https://rules.sos.ri.gov/regulations/Part/450-00-00-7', 'df846ba176cd6739d63564d7699c736ba92fe468e63695e55dd48d1d2ac692c3', 'Incorporated Materials A. The Fire Safety Code Board of Appeal and Review hereby adopts and incorporates as the RIFC the provisions of the National Fire Protection Association (NFPA) 1, Fire Code, 2021 edition, with annexes, as published by the NFPA not including any further editions or amendments thereof and only to the extent that the provisions therein are not inconsistent with R.I. Gen. Laws', 'Quote re-checked word for word on the official page by the Academy source check.'),
  ('jurisdiction', 'RI', '2026-11-22T02:26:12Z'::timestamptz, 'official_text', 'verified', 'https://webserver.rilegislature.gov/Statutes/TITLE23/23-27.3/23-27.3-100.1.7.htm', null, 'The local building codes and ordinances shall remain in effect until the adoption of the state building code, July 1, 1977, and the local cities and towns shall be prohibited from enacting any local building codes and ordinances in the future.', 'Statewide code model, re-checked on the official page.'),
  ('adoption', (md5('academykb:adoption:st:SC:ibc:2021')::uuid)::text, '2026-11-22T02:26:12Z'::timestamptz, 'official_text', 'verified', 'https://llr.sc.gov/bcc/PDFfiles/Building%20Codes%20in%20Effect%20for%20South%20Carolina%20Final.pdf', 'b2ad8acd6ce54d1f1ba015a905ed5e1253f4cb03ad3ba5ff4bd85c358767ce11', 'The Council established the implementation date for local jurisdictions as January 1, 2023. The adopted modifications and the mandatory codes are as follows: ... 2021 South Carolina Building Code or the 2021 International Building Code with SC modifications', 'Quote re-checked word for word on the official page by the Academy source check.'),
  ('adoption', (md5('academykb:adoption:st:SC:irc:2021')::uuid)::text, '2026-11-22T02:26:12Z'::timestamptz, 'official_text', 'verified', 'https://llr.sc.gov/bcc/PDFfiles/Building%20Codes%20in%20Effect%20for%20South%20Carolina%20Final.pdf', 'b2ad8acd6ce54d1f1ba015a905ed5e1253f4cb03ad3ba5ff4bd85c358767ce11', 'The Council established the implementation date for local jurisdictions as January 1, 2023. The adopted modifications and the mandatory codes are as follows: ... 2021 South Carolina Residential Code or the 2021 International Residential Code with SC modifications', 'Quote re-checked word for word on the official page by the Academy source check.'),
  ('adoption', (md5('academykb:adoption:st:SC:ifc:2021')::uuid)::text, '2026-11-22T02:26:12Z'::timestamptz, 'official_text', 'verified', 'https://llr.sc.gov/bcc/PDFfiles/Building%20Codes%20in%20Effect%20for%20South%20Carolina%20Final.pdf', 'b2ad8acd6ce54d1f1ba015a905ed5e1253f4cb03ad3ba5ff4bd85c358767ce11', 'The Council established the implementation date for local jurisdictions as January 1, 2023. The adopted modifications and the mandatory codes are as follows: ... 2021 South Carolina Fire Code or the 2021 International Fire Code with SC modifications', 'Quote re-checked word for word on the official page by the Academy source check.'),
  ('adoption', (md5('academykb:adoption:st:SC:ipc:2021')::uuid)::text, '2026-11-22T02:26:12Z'::timestamptz, 'official_text', 'verified', 'https://llr.sc.gov/bcc/PDFfiles/Building%20Codes%20in%20Effect%20for%20South%20Carolina%20Final.pdf', 'b2ad8acd6ce54d1f1ba015a905ed5e1253f4cb03ad3ba5ff4bd85c358767ce11', 'The Council established the implementation date for local jurisdictions as January 1, 2023. The adopted modifications and the mandatory codes are as follows: ... 2021 South Carolina Plumbing Code or the 2021 International Plumbing Code with SC modifications', 'Quote re-checked word for word on the official page by the Academy source check.'),
  ('adoption', (md5('academykb:adoption:st:SC:imc:2021')::uuid)::text, '2026-11-22T02:26:12Z'::timestamptz, 'official_text', 'verified', 'https://llr.sc.gov/bcc/PDFfiles/Building%20Codes%20in%20Effect%20for%20South%20Carolina%20Final.pdf', 'b2ad8acd6ce54d1f1ba015a905ed5e1253f4cb03ad3ba5ff4bd85c358767ce11', 'The Council established the implementation date for local jurisdictions as January 1, 2023. The adopted modifications and the mandatory codes are as follows: ... 2021 South Carolina Mechanical Code or the 2021 International Mechanical Code with SC modifications', 'Quote re-checked word for word on the official page by the Academy source check.'),
  ('adoption', (md5('academykb:adoption:st:SC:ifgc:2021')::uuid)::text, '2026-11-22T02:26:12Z'::timestamptz, 'official_text', 'verified', 'https://llr.sc.gov/bcc/PDFfiles/Building%20Codes%20in%20Effect%20for%20South%20Carolina%20Final.pdf', 'b2ad8acd6ce54d1f1ba015a905ed5e1253f4cb03ad3ba5ff4bd85c358767ce11', 'The Council established the implementation date for local jurisdictions as January 1, 2023. The adopted modifications and the mandatory codes are as follows: ... 2021 South Carolina Fuel Gas Code or the 2021 International Fuel Gas Code with SC modifications', 'Quote re-checked word for word on the official page by the Academy source check.'),
  ('adoption', (md5('academykb:adoption:st:SC:nec:2020')::uuid)::text, '2026-11-22T02:26:12Z'::timestamptz, 'official_text', 'verified', 'https://llr.sc.gov/bcc/PDFfiles/Building%20Codes%20in%20Effect%20for%20South%20Carolina%20Final.pdf', 'b2ad8acd6ce54d1f1ba015a905ed5e1253f4cb03ad3ba5ff4bd85c358767ce11', 'The Council established the implementation date for local jurisdictions as January 1, 2023. The adopted modifications and the mandatory codes are as follows: ... 2020 National Electrical Code (NFPA 70) with SC modifications', 'Quote re-checked word for word on the official page by the Academy source check.'),
  ('adoption', (md5('academykb:adoption:st:SC:iecc:2009')::uuid)::text, '2026-11-22T02:26:12Z'::timestamptz, 'official_text', 'verified', 'https://llr.sc.gov/bcc/PDFfiles/2024%20Code%20Adoption%20Notice.pdf', '8347c8557e516dda97626122d215227b40cd77e136726d5ede93636010702c4d', 'The South Carolina Legislature has enacted the Energy Standard Act (S.C. Code Ann. § 6-10-10 et seq.), and pursuant to the Energy Standard Act, the 2009 edition of the International Energy Conservation Code has been statutorily adopted as the energy standard and is mandatory for use in all jurisdictions within the State.', 'Quote re-checked word for word on the official page by the Academy source check.'),
  ('jurisdiction', 'SC', '2026-11-22T02:26:12Z'::timestamptz, 'official_text', 'verified', 'https://llr.sc.gov/bcc/PDFfiles/Building%20Codes%20in%20Effect%20for%20South%20Carolina%20Final.pdf', null, 'The mandatory codes referenced in S.C, Ann. §6-9-50(1976, as amended), modified and adopted by the South Carolina Building Codes Council (Council), must be enforced by every South Carolina municipality and county.', 'Statewide code model, re-checked on the official page.'),
  ('adoption', (md5('academykb:adoption:st:TN:irc:2018')::uuid)::text, '2026-11-22T02:26:12Z'::timestamptz, 'official_text', 'verified', 'https://publications.tnsosfiles.com/rules/0780/0780-02/0780-02-23.20260923.pdf', '4cc7cb30254ef5a8ab94b151f52a5aa29c40b56d33ddf24fa2b61636fea46ead', '(a) International Residential Code (IRC), 2018 edition, published by the International Code Council, Inc. (ICC), ... Amendments filed April 17, 2020; effective July 16, 2020.', 'Quote re-checked word for word on the official page by the Academy source check.'),
  ('adoption', (md5('academykb:adoption:st:TN:iecc:2018')::uuid)::text, '2026-11-22T02:26:12Z'::timestamptz, 'official_text', 'verified', 'https://publications.tnsosfiles.com/rules/0780/0780-02/0780-02-23.20260923.pdf', '4cc7cb30254ef5a8ab94b151f52a5aa29c40b56d33ddf24fa2b61636fea46ead', '(b) International Energy Conservation Code (IECC), 2018 edition, published by the ICC, except that: ... Amendments filed April 17, 2020; effective July 16, 2020.', 'Quote re-checked word for word on the official page by the Academy source check.'),
  ('adoption', (md5('academykb:adoption:st:TN:ibc:2021')::uuid)::text, '2026-11-22T02:26:12Z'::timestamptz, 'official_text', 'verified', 'https://publications.tnsosfiles.com/rules/0780/0780-02/0780-02-02.20250417.pdf', '4036d7ab01c125a87a140831cd87ffc1f4284f9bf351795ac0c8e5617e7b2093', '(a) The International Building Code (IBC), 2021 edition, published by the International Code Council (ICC), except for the following changes: ... Amendments filed January 17, 2025; effective April 17, 2025.', 'Quote re-checked word for word on the official page by the Academy source check.'),
  ('adoption', (md5('academykb:adoption:st:TN:ifgc:2021')::uuid)::text, '2026-11-22T02:26:12Z'::timestamptz, 'official_text', 'verified', 'https://publications.tnsosfiles.com/rules/0780/0780-02/0780-02-02.20250417.pdf', '4036d7ab01c125a87a140831cd87ffc1f4284f9bf351795ac0c8e5617e7b2093', '(b) The International Fuel Gas Code (IFGC), 2021 edition, published by the International Code Council (ICC). ... Amendments filed January 17, 2025; effective April 17, 2025.', 'Quote re-checked word for word on the official page by the Academy source check.'),
  ('adoption', (md5('academykb:adoption:st:TN:imc:2021')::uuid)::text, '2026-11-22T02:26:12Z'::timestamptz, 'official_text', 'verified', 'https://publications.tnsosfiles.com/rules/0780/0780-02/0780-02-02.20250417.pdf', '4036d7ab01c125a87a140831cd87ffc1f4284f9bf351795ac0c8e5617e7b2093', '(c) The International Mechanical Code (IMC), 2021 edition, published by the International Code Council (ICC). ... Amendments filed January 17, 2025; effective April 17, 2025.', 'Quote re-checked word for word on the official page by the Academy source check.'),
  ('adoption', (md5('academykb:adoption:st:TN:ipc:2021')::uuid)::text, '2026-11-22T02:26:12Z'::timestamptz, 'official_text', 'verified', 'https://publications.tnsosfiles.com/rules/0780/0780-02/0780-02-02.20250417.pdf', '4036d7ab01c125a87a140831cd87ffc1f4284f9bf351795ac0c8e5617e7b2093', '(d) The International Plumbing Code (IPC), 2021 edition, published by the International Code Council (ICC). ... Amendments filed January 17, 2025; effective April 17, 2025.', 'Quote re-checked word for word on the official page by the Academy source check.'),
  ('adoption', (md5('academykb:adoption:st:TN:ifc:2021')::uuid)::text, '2026-11-22T02:26:12Z'::timestamptz, 'official_text', 'verified', 'https://publications.tnsosfiles.com/rules/0780/0780-02/0780-02-02.20250417.pdf', '4036d7ab01c125a87a140831cd87ffc1f4284f9bf351795ac0c8e5617e7b2093', '(f) The International Fire Code (IFC), 2021 edition, published by the International Code Council (ICC), except for the following changes: ... Amendments filed January 17, 2025; effective April 17, 2025.', 'Quote re-checked word for word on the official page by the Academy source check.'),
  ('adoption', (md5('academykb:adoption:st:TN:iecc:2021')::uuid)::text, '2026-11-22T02:26:12Z'::timestamptz, 'official_text', 'verified', 'https://publications.tnsosfiles.com/rules/0780/0780-02/0780-02-02.20250417.pdf', '4036d7ab01c125a87a140831cd87ffc1f4284f9bf351795ac0c8e5617e7b2093', '(g) The International Energy Conservation Code (IECC), 2021 edition, published by the International Code Council (ICC), except for the following changes: ... Amendments filed January 17, 2025; effective April 17, 2025.', 'Quote re-checked word for word on the official page by the Academy source check.'),
  ('adoption', (md5('academykb:adoption:st:TN:iebc:2021')::uuid)::text, '2026-11-22T02:26:12Z'::timestamptz, 'official_text', 'verified', 'https://publications.tnsosfiles.com/rules/0780/0780-02/0780-02-02.20250417.pdf', '4036d7ab01c125a87a140831cd87ffc1f4284f9bf351795ac0c8e5617e7b2093', '(h) The International Existing Building Code (IEBC), 2021 edition, published by the International Code Council (ICC), except for the following changes: ... Amendments filed January 17, 2025; effective April 17, 2025.', 'Quote re-checked word for word on the official page by the Academy source check.'),
  ('adoption', (md5('academykb:adoption:st:TN:nec:2017')::uuid)::text, '2026-11-22T02:26:12Z'::timestamptz, 'official_text', 'verified', 'https://publications.tnsosfiles.com/rules/0780/0780-02/0780-02-01.20250714.pdf', 'b034ac0cea3f99fc81c7b653df983699aceff5587655e9eece589f601e5af74a', 'those prescribed in the National Electrical Code, 2017 edition, published by the National Fire Protection Association, 1 Batterymarch Park, Quincy, Massachusetts 02169, effective October 1, 2018, except that:', 'Quote re-checked word for word on the official page by the Academy source check.'),
  ('jurisdiction', 'TN', '2026-11-22T02:26:12Z'::timestamptz, 'official_text', 'verified', 'https://publications.tnsosfiles.com/rules/0780/0780-02/0780-02-23.20260923.pdf', null, 'No construction of a one (1) or two (2) family dwelling or townhouse shall be started without securing a building permit from an issuing agent authorized by the Commissioner of Commerce and Insurance, except in an exempt jurisdiction or in the unincorporated areas of a county or in a municipality that have opted out of these provisions.', 'Statewide code model, re-checked on the official page.'),
  ('adoption', (md5('academykb:adoption:st:TX:irc:2012')::uuid)::text, '2026-11-22T02:26:12Z'::timestamptz, 'official_text', 'verified', 'https://tcss.legis.texas.gov/resources/LG/htm/LG.214.htm', '3b12de334810d8373fa0b045c075d6cee729bfba7a27eb88669e3cafcd527230', 'Sec. 214.212. INTERNATIONAL RESIDENTIAL CODE. (a) To protect the public health, safety, and welfare, the International Residential Code, as it existed on May 1, 2012, is adopted as a municipal residential building code in this state. (b) The International Residential Code applies to all construction, alteration, remodeling, enlargement, and repair of residential structures in a municipality.', 'Quote re-checked word for word on the official page by the Academy source check.'),
  ('adoption', (md5('academykb:adoption:st:TX:ibc:2012')::uuid)::text, '2026-11-22T02:26:12Z'::timestamptz, 'official_text', 'verified', 'https://tcss.legis.texas.gov/resources/LG/htm/LG.214.htm', '3b12de334810d8373fa0b045c075d6cee729bfba7a27eb88669e3cafcd527230', 'Sec. 214.216. INTERNATIONAL BUILDING CODE. (a) To protect the public health, safety, and welfare, the International Building Code, as it existed on May 1, 2012, is adopted as a municipal commercial building code in this state. (b) The International Building Code applies to all commercial buildings in a municipality and to any alteration, remodeling, enlargement, or repair of those commercial buildings.', 'Quote re-checked word for word on the official page by the Academy source check.'),
  ('adoption', (md5('academykb:adoption:st:TX:iecc:2015')::uuid)::text, '2026-11-22T02:26:12Z'::timestamptz, 'official_text', 'verified', 'https://comptroller.texas.gov/programs/seco/code/single-family.php', '60b12571a73f5af0b8187d5679e7f0424dceded263b6b5014e39d31488d73c5d', 'Effective Sept. 1, 2016, SECO adopted the Energy Efficiency Chapter 11 of the 2015 International Residential Code (IRC) as the state’s Building Energy Efficiency Performance Standards for residential construction (i.e., one- and two-family residences three stories or fewer above grade).', 'Quote re-checked word for word on the official page by the Academy source check.'),
  ('adoption', (md5('academykb:adoption:st:TX:iecc:2015')::uuid)::text, '2026-11-22T02:26:12Z'::timestamptz, 'official_text', 'verified', 'https://comptroller.texas.gov/programs/seco/code/commercial.php', 'ea88efe23b1bfbafd106de86128a533b15e8ee847c464cb730f89418b52a9ff0', 'Effective Nov. 1, 2016, SECO adopted the 2015 International Energy Conservation Code (IECC) for commercial, industrial and residential buildings taller than three stories.', 'Quote re-checked word for word on the official page by the Academy source check.'),
  ('adoption', (md5('academykb:adoption:st:TX:nec:2026')::uuid)::text, '2026-11-22T02:26:12Z'::timestamptz, 'official_text', 'verified', 'https://www.tdlr.texas.gov/news/rulemaking/2026/09/01/commission-adopts-rules-12/', 'ac8ad9a81c834b957a1b638322720a06007df4aa8b8ce595c891b24a55ed307e', 'The adopted amendments adopt the 2026 National Electrical Code as the state electrical code, with a limited exception pertaining to ground-fault circuit interrupter requirements for certain outdoor outlets. The adoption justification was published in the August 28, 2026, issue of the Texas Register (51 TexReg 5776). The updated rule chapter will be available in the Texas Administrative Code upon its effective date of September 1, 2026.', 'Quote re-checked word for word on the official page by the Academy source check.'),
  ('adoption', (md5('academykb:adoption:st:TX:upc:2021')::uuid)::text, '2026-11-22T02:26:12Z'::timestamptz, 'official_text', 'verified', 'https://www.sos.state.tx.us/texreg/archive/November132026/Adopted%20Rules/22.EXAMINING%20BOARDS.html', 'c599dacafa2764535ab54d1ec1613ffc1f6207032a029a252890791397154c97', 'The Texas State Board of Plumbing Examiners (Board) adopts the amendment to 22 Texas Administrative Code (TAC), Chapter 367, §367.2 which updates the codes adopted under the authority of Texas Occupations Code, Sec. 1301.255 to the 2021 Uniform Plumbing Code and the 2021 International Plumbing Code. ... Effective date: November 19, 2026', 'Quote re-checked word for word on the official page by the Academy source check.'),
  ('adoption', (md5('academykb:adoption:st:TX:ipc:2021')::uuid)::text, '2026-11-22T02:26:12Z'::timestamptz, 'official_text', 'verified', 'https://www.sos.state.tx.us/texreg/archive/November132026/Adopted%20Rules/22.EXAMINING%20BOARDS.html', 'c599dacafa2764535ab54d1ec1613ffc1f6207032a029a252890791397154c97', '(2) the 2021 International Plumbing Code, as published by the International Code Council and the codes incorporated by reference within the 2021 International Plumbing Code, including: (A) the 2021 International Fuel Gas Code; and (B) the 2021 International Residential Code. ... Effective date: November 19, 2026', 'Quote re-checked word for word on the official page by the Academy source check.'),
  ('jurisdiction', 'TX', '2026-11-22T02:26:12Z'::timestamptz, 'official_text', 'verified', 'https://tcss.legis.texas.gov/resources/LG/htm/LG.214.htm', null, 'Sec. 214.212. INTERNATIONAL RESIDENTIAL CODE. (a) To protect the public health, safety, and welfare, the International Residential Code, as it existed on May 1, 2012, is adopted as a municipal residential building code in this state. (b) The International Residential Code applies to all construction, alteration, remodeling, enlargement, and repair of residential structures in a municipality.', 'Statewide code model, re-checked on the official page.'),
  ('adoption', (md5('academykb:adoption:st:UT:ibc:2024')::uuid)::text, '2026-11-22T02:26:12Z'::timestamptz, 'official_text', 'verified', 'https://le.utah.gov/xcode/Title15A/Chapter2/C15A-2-S103_2026050620260701.html', '0494674f98799fa2c474d6ff01e34f526f6d8d8008200f1794cbdd6f55868b6e', '(1) Subject to the other provisions of this part, the following construction codes are incorporated by reference, and together with the amendments specified in Chapter 3, ... are the construction standards to be applied to building construction, alteration, remodeling, and repair, ... in the state: (a) the 2024 edition of the International Building Code, including Appendices C and J, issued by the International Code Council; [Utah Code section header: ''(Effective 7/1/2026)'']', 'Quote re-checked word for word on the official page by the Academy source check.'),
  ('adoption', (md5('academykb:adoption:st:UT:irc:2021')::uuid)::text, '2026-11-22T02:26:12Z'::timestamptz, 'official_text', 'verified', 'https://le.utah.gov/xcode/Title15A/Chapter2/C15A-2-S103_2026050620260701.html', '0494674f98799fa2c474d6ff01e34f526f6d8d8008200f1794cbdd6f55868b6e', '(1) Subject to the other provisions of this part, the following construction codes are incorporated by reference, and together with the amendments specified in Chapter 3, ... are the construction standards to be applied to building construction, alteration, remodeling, and repair, ... in the state: (b) the 2021 edition of the International Residential Code, issued by the International Code Council; [Utah Code section header: ''(Effective 7/1/2026)'']', 'Quote re-checked word for word on the official page by the Academy source check.'),
  ('adoption', (md5('academykb:adoption:st:UT:iebc:2024')::uuid)::text, '2026-11-22T02:26:12Z'::timestamptz, 'official_text', 'verified', 'https://le.utah.gov/xcode/Title15A/Chapter2/C15A-2-S103_2026050620260701.html', '0494674f98799fa2c474d6ff01e34f526f6d8d8008200f1794cbdd6f55868b6e', '(1) Subject to the other provisions of this part, the following construction codes are incorporated by reference, and together with the amendments specified in Chapter 3, ... are the construction standards to be applied to building construction, alteration, remodeling, and repair, ... in the state: (i) the 2024 edition of the International Existing Building Code, issued by the International Code Council; [Utah Code section header: ''(Effective 7/1/2026)'']', 'Quote re-checked word for word on the official page by the Academy source check.'),
  ('adoption', (md5('academykb:adoption:st:UT:ipc:2024')::uuid)::text, '2026-11-22T02:26:12Z'::timestamptz, 'official_text', 'verified', 'https://le.utah.gov/xcode/Title15A/Chapter2/C15A-2-S103_2026050620260701.html', '0494674f98799fa2c474d6ff01e34f526f6d8d8008200f1794cbdd6f55868b6e', '(1) Subject to the other provisions of this part, the following construction codes are incorporated by reference, and together with the amendments specified in Chapter 3, ... are the construction standards to be applied to building construction, alteration, remodeling, and repair, ... in the state: (d) the 2024 edition of the International Plumbing Code, issued by the International Code Council; [Utah Code section header: ''(Effective 7/1/2026)'']', 'Quote re-checked word for word on the official page by the Academy source check.'),
  ('adoption', (md5('academykb:adoption:st:UT:imc:2024')::uuid)::text, '2026-11-22T02:26:12Z'::timestamptz, 'official_text', 'verified', 'https://le.utah.gov/xcode/Title15A/Chapter2/C15A-2-S103_2026050620260701.html', '0494674f98799fa2c474d6ff01e34f526f6d8d8008200f1794cbdd6f55868b6e', '(1) Subject to the other provisions of this part, the following construction codes are incorporated by reference, and together with the amendments specified in Chapter 3, ... are the construction standards to be applied to building construction, alteration, remodeling, and repair, ... in the state: (e) the 2024 edition of the International Mechanical Code, issued by the International Code Council; [Utah Code section header: ''(Effective 7/1/2026)'']', 'Quote re-checked word for word on the official page by the Academy source check.'),
  ('adoption', (md5('academykb:adoption:st:UT:ifgc:2024')::uuid)::text, '2026-11-22T02:26:12Z'::timestamptz, 'official_text', 'verified', 'https://le.utah.gov/xcode/Title15A/Chapter2/C15A-2-S103_2026050620260701.html', '0494674f98799fa2c474d6ff01e34f526f6d8d8008200f1794cbdd6f55868b6e', '(1) Subject to the other provisions of this part, the following construction codes are incorporated by reference, and together with the amendments specified in Chapter 3, ... are the construction standards to be applied to building construction, alteration, remodeling, and repair, ... in the state: (f) the 2024 edition of the International Fuel Gas Code, issued by the International Code Council; [Utah Code section header: ''(Effective 7/1/2026)'']', 'Quote re-checked word for word on the official page by the Academy source check.'),
  ('adoption', (md5('academykb:adoption:st:UT:iecc:2024')::uuid)::text, '2026-11-22T02:26:12Z'::timestamptz, 'official_text', 'verified', 'https://le.utah.gov/xcode/Title15A/Chapter2/C15A-2-S103_2026050620260701.html', '0494674f98799fa2c474d6ff01e34f526f6d8d8008200f1794cbdd6f55868b6e', '(1) Subject to the other provisions of this part, the following construction codes are incorporated by reference, and together with the amendments specified in Chapter 3, ... are the construction standards to be applied to building construction, alteration, remodeling, and repair, ... in the state: (h) the 2024 edition of the International Energy Conservation Code, issued by the International Code Council; [Utah Code section header: ''(Effective 7/1/2026)'']', 'Quote re-checked word for word on the official page by the Academy source check.'),
  ('adoption', (md5('academykb:adoption:st:UT:nec:2023')::uuid)::text, '2026-11-22T02:26:12Z'::timestamptz, 'official_text', 'verified', 'https://le.utah.gov/xcode/Title15A/Chapter2/C15A-2-S103_2026050620260701.html', '0494674f98799fa2c474d6ff01e34f526f6d8d8008200f1794cbdd6f55868b6e', '(1) Subject to the other provisions of this part, the following construction codes are incorporated by reference, and together with the amendments specified in Chapter 3, ... are the construction standards to be applied to building construction, alteration, remodeling, and repair, ... in the state: (g) the 2023 edition of the National Electrical Code, issued by the National Fire Protection Association; [Utah Code section header: ''(Effective 7/1/2026)'']', 'Quote re-checked word for word on the official page by the Academy source check.'),
  ('adoption', (md5('academykb:adoption:st:UT:ifc:2024')::uuid)::text, '2026-11-22T02:26:12Z'::timestamptz, 'official_text', 'verified', 'https://le.utah.gov/xcode/Title15A/Chapter5/C15A-5-S103_2026050620260701.html', '7d98114cb02a18fc6c276ada36d84d4d1ca25514297ca500ad6d6093128c7a9e', '15A-5-103. Nationally recognized codes incorporated by reference. The following codes are incorporated by reference into the State Fire Code: (1) the International Fire Code, 2024 edition, excluding appendices, as issued by the International Code Council, Inc., except as amended by Part 2, Statewide Amendments and Additions to International Fire Code Incorporated as Part of State Fire Code; [Section header: ''(Effective 7/1/2026)'']', 'Quote re-checked word for word on the official page by the Academy source check.'),
  ('jurisdiction', 'UT', '2026-11-22T02:26:12Z'::timestamptz, 'official_text', 'verified', 'https://le.utah.gov/xcode/Title15A/Chapter1/C15A-1-S204_2025110620251206.html', null, '(1) (a) The State Construction Code is the construction codes adopted with any modifications in accordance with this section that the state and each political subdivision of the state shall follow.', 'Statewide code model, re-checked on the official page.'),
  ('adoption', (md5('academykb:adoption:st:VA:ibc:2021')::uuid)::text, '2026-11-22T02:26:12Z'::timestamptz, 'official_text', 'verified', 'https://law.lis.virginia.gov/admincode/title13/agency5/chapter63/section10/', '7d4f91e8915bed5333b1ac1e9d320288686946f7730cddc5c3a70dceba752d36', 'Note: This code is also known as the 2021 edition of the USBC due to the use of the 2021 editions of the model codes. B. Section 101.2 Incorporation by reference. Chapters 2 - 35 of the 2021 International Building Code, published by the International Code Council, Inc., are adopted and incorporated by reference to be an enforceable part of the USBC.', 'Quote re-checked word for word on the official page by the Academy source check.'),
  ('adoption', (md5('academykb:adoption:st:VA:irc:2021')::uuid)::text, '2026-11-22T02:26:12Z'::timestamptz, 'official_text', 'verified', 'https://law.lis.virginia.gov/admincode/title13/agency5/chapter63/section10/', '7d4f91e8915bed5333b1ac1e9d320288686946f7730cddc5c3a70dceba752d36', 'Note 1: The IBC references other International Codes and standards, including the following major codes: 2021 International Plumbing Code (IPC) 2021 International Mechanical Code (IMC) 2020 National Fire Protection Association (NFPA) 70 2021 International Fuel Gas Code (IFGC) 2021 International Energy Conservation Code (IECC) 2021 International Residential Code (IRC) Note 2: The IRC is applicable to the construction of detached one-family and two-family dwellings and townhouses as set out in Section 310.', 'Quote re-checked word for word on the official page by the Academy source check.'),
  ('adoption', (md5('academykb:adoption:st:VA:ipc:2021')::uuid)::text, '2026-11-22T02:26:12Z'::timestamptz, 'official_text', 'verified', 'https://law.lis.virginia.gov/admincode/title13/agency5/chapter63/section10/', '7d4f91e8915bed5333b1ac1e9d320288686946f7730cddc5c3a70dceba752d36', 'Note 1: The IBC references other International Codes and standards, including the following major codes: 2021 International Plumbing Code (IPC) 2021 International Mechanical Code (IMC) 2020 National Fire Protection Association (NFPA) 70 2021 International Fuel Gas Code (IFGC) 2021 International Energy Conservation Code (IECC) 2021 International Residential Code (IRC)', 'Quote re-checked word for word on the official page by the Academy source check.'),
  ('adoption', (md5('academykb:adoption:st:VA:imc:2021')::uuid)::text, '2026-11-22T02:26:12Z'::timestamptz, 'official_text', 'verified', 'https://law.lis.virginia.gov/admincode/title13/agency5/chapter63/section10/', '7d4f91e8915bed5333b1ac1e9d320288686946f7730cddc5c3a70dceba752d36', 'Note 1: The IBC references other International Codes and standards, including the following major codes: 2021 International Plumbing Code (IPC) 2021 International Mechanical Code (IMC) 2020 National Fire Protection Association (NFPA) 70 2021 International Fuel Gas Code (IFGC) 2021 International Energy Conservation Code (IECC) 2021 International Residential Code (IRC)', 'Quote re-checked word for word on the official page by the Academy source check.'),
  ('adoption', (md5('academykb:adoption:st:VA:ifgc:2021')::uuid)::text, '2026-11-22T02:26:12Z'::timestamptz, 'official_text', 'verified', 'https://law.lis.virginia.gov/admincode/title13/agency5/chapter63/section10/', '7d4f91e8915bed5333b1ac1e9d320288686946f7730cddc5c3a70dceba752d36', 'Note 1: The IBC references other International Codes and standards, including the following major codes: 2021 International Plumbing Code (IPC) 2021 International Mechanical Code (IMC) 2020 National Fire Protection Association (NFPA) 70 2021 International Fuel Gas Code (IFGC) 2021 International Energy Conservation Code (IECC) 2021 International Residential Code (IRC)', 'Quote re-checked word for word on the official page by the Academy source check.'),
  ('adoption', (md5('academykb:adoption:st:VA:iecc:2021')::uuid)::text, '2026-11-22T02:26:12Z'::timestamptz, 'official_text', 'verified', 'https://law.lis.virginia.gov/admincode/title13/agency5/chapter63/section10/', '7d4f91e8915bed5333b1ac1e9d320288686946f7730cddc5c3a70dceba752d36', 'Note 1: The IBC references other International Codes and standards, including the following major codes: 2021 International Plumbing Code (IPC) 2021 International Mechanical Code (IMC) 2020 National Fire Protection Association (NFPA) 70 2021 International Fuel Gas Code (IFGC) 2021 International Energy Conservation Code (IECC) 2021 International Residential Code (IRC)', 'Quote re-checked word for word on the official page by the Academy source check.'),
  ('adoption', (md5('academykb:adoption:st:VA:nec:2020')::uuid)::text, '2026-11-22T02:26:12Z'::timestamptz, 'official_text', 'verified', 'https://www.dhcd.virginia.gov/codes', '2edfb0ecbe56693c811f346d096fc63c3f506e5c855d778210e6993198b2e7ab', 'Effective January 18, 2024, Virginia adopted the 2021 I-codes as referenced in the Virginia Construction Part 1 and the 2021 Statewide Fire Prevention Code; and the 2020 National Electrical Code.', 'Quote re-checked word for word on the official page by the Academy source check.'),
  ('adoption', (md5('academykb:adoption:st:VA:iebc:2021')::uuid)::text, '2026-11-22T02:26:12Z'::timestamptz, 'official_text', 'verified', 'https://law.lis.virginia.gov/admincodefull/title13/agency5/chapter63/partII/', '29fdf5d90ea6cf3b94b5aea30380e4ebc269f33dc0e25ebea940a11a545dab10', 'B. Section 101.2 Incorporation by reference. Chapters 2 through 16 of the 2021 International Existing Building Code, published by the International Code Council, Inc., are adopted and incorporated by reference to be an enforceable part of the VEBC.', 'Quote re-checked word for word on the official page by the Academy source check.'),
  ('adoption', (md5('academykb:adoption:st:VA:ifc:2021')::uuid)::text, '2026-11-22T02:26:12Z'::timestamptz, 'official_text', 'verified', 'https://law.lis.virginia.gov/admincodefull/title13/agency5/chapter52/', '9b9b09d8dd6e9eb09284359342e63d30e4ce43a8f30b54fd2d517385340c7148', '13VAC5-52-30. Section 103 Incorporation by reference. A. 103.1 General. The following document is adopted and incorporated by reference to be an enforceable part of the SFPC: The International Fire Code -- 2021 Edition, hereinafter referred to as "IFC," published by the International Code Council, Inc.', 'Quote re-checked word for word on the official page by the Academy source check.'),
  ('jurisdiction', 'VA', '2026-11-22T02:26:12Z'::timestamptz, 'official_text', 'verified', 'https://law.lis.virginia.gov/vacode/title36/chapter6/section36-105/', null, 'A. Enforcement generally. Enforcement of the provisions of the Building Code for construction and rehabilitation shall be the responsibility of the local building department.', 'Statewide code model, re-checked on the official page.'),
  ('adoption', (md5('academykb:adoption:st:VT:ibc:2021')::uuid)::text, '2026-11-22T02:26:12Z'::timestamptz, 'official_text', 'verified', 'https://firesafety.vermont.gov/sites/firesafety/files/Rules/2025%20Vermont%20Fire%20%26%20Building%20Safety%20Code.pdf', '2a9aff05a1d714489c4409bff018b41b074d65e92a9c0fc6b2d3cda23e75e924', 'Section 2 Adoption of National Recognized Codes The following nationally recognized safety standards, as amended herein, are adopted to make rules regarding the safeguarding of people and property in case of fire, explosion, hazardous materials, dangerous structural conditions, and the generation of carbon monoxide. LIFE SAFETY CODE – NFPA 101 – 2021 FIRE CODE – NFPA 1 – 2021 INTERNATIONAL BUILDING CODE – IBC – 2021 INTERNATIONAL EXISTING BUILDING CODE – IEBC – 2021', 'Quote re-checked word for word on the official page by the Academy source check.'),
  ('adoption', (md5('academykb:adoption:st:VT:iebc:2021')::uuid)::text, '2026-11-22T02:26:12Z'::timestamptz, 'official_text', 'verified', 'https://firesafety.vermont.gov/sites/firesafety/files/Rules/2025%20Vermont%20Fire%20%26%20Building%20Safety%20Code.pdf', '2a9aff05a1d714489c4409bff018b41b074d65e92a9c0fc6b2d3cda23e75e924', 'Section 2 Adoption of National Recognized Codes The following nationally recognized safety standards, as amended herein, are adopted to make rules regarding the safeguarding of people and property in case of fire, explosion, hazardous materials, dangerous structural conditions, and the generation of carbon monoxide. LIFE SAFETY CODE – NFPA 101 – 2021 FIRE CODE – NFPA 1 – 2021 INTERNATIONAL BUILDING CODE – IBC – 2021 INTERNATIONAL EXISTING BUILDING CODE – IEBC – 2021', 'Quote re-checked word for word on the official page by the Academy source check.'),
  ('adoption', (md5('academykb:adoption:st:VT:nfpa1:2021')::uuid)::text, '2026-11-22T02:26:12Z'::timestamptz, 'official_text', 'verified', 'https://firesafety.vermont.gov/sites/firesafety/files/Rules/2025%20Vermont%20Fire%20%26%20Building%20Safety%20Code.pdf', '2a9aff05a1d714489c4409bff018b41b074d65e92a9c0fc6b2d3cda23e75e924', 'Section 2 Adoption of National Recognized Codes The following nationally recognized safety standards, as amended herein, are adopted to make rules regarding the safeguarding of people and property in case of fire, explosion, hazardous materials, dangerous structural conditions, and the generation of carbon monoxide. LIFE SAFETY CODE – NFPA 101 – 2021 FIRE CODE – NFPA 1 – 2021 INTERNATIONAL BUILDING CODE – IBC – 2021 INTERNATIONAL EXISTING BUILDING CODE – IEBC – 2021', 'Quote re-checked word for word on the official page by the Academy source check.'),
  ('adoption', (md5('academykb:adoption:st:VT:nec:2023')::uuid)::text, '2026-11-22T02:26:12Z'::timestamptz, 'official_text', 'verified', 'https://firesafety.vermont.gov/sites/firesafety/files/Rules/2025%20Vermont%20Electrical%20Safety%20Rules.pdf', '26918d41940515ebf36270e65e8ac0476861b238890a9e9f5f6a9edf725744f7', 'NFPA 70, National Electrical Code, (2023 edition) To meet the needs and concerns of Vermonters, and Electricians. NFPA 70 is amended as follows:', 'Quote re-checked word for word on the official page by the Academy source check.'),
  ('adoption', (md5('academykb:adoption:st:VT:ipc:2024')::uuid)::text, '2026-11-22T02:26:12Z'::timestamptz, 'official_text', 'verified', 'https://firesafety.vermont.gov/sites/firesafety/files/Rules/2025%20Vermont%20Plumbing%20Rules%20V2.pdf', '492048b4d891d4109fc6eebe22ccec51bb5f70ad8a2db67b253e40369769667c', 'Under 26 V.S.A. Section 2173, the Board adopts the provisions of the 2024 International Plumbing Code (hereinafter referred to as 2024 IPC). All plumbing installations shall comply with the 2024 IPC, as amended in this section to meet the individual needs of Vermont.', 'Quote re-checked word for word on the official page by the Academy source check.'),
  ('adoption', (md5('academykb:adoption:st:VT:state_energy:vermont-residential-building-energy-standards-rbes')::uuid)::text, '2026-11-22T02:26:12Z'::timestamptz, 'official_text', 'verified', 'https://publicservice.vermont.gov/efficiency/building-energy-standards/residential-building-energy-standards', '2f30bbb2257ec7565d22a325c6875daba2d4cee9bf0709c5f506d215e38deadf', 'The new RBES Rule was adopted on April 10, 2026 with an effective date of July 14, 2026 . These updates allow compliance with either the 2020 or 2024 versions of the RBES. The changes provide much needed flexibility and cost reduction opportunities, to help address Vermont’s significant housing shortage. The 2020 and 2024 RBES apply to all new residential construction, including additions, alterations, renovations, and repairs.', 'Quote re-checked word for word on the official page by the Academy source check.'),
  ('adoption', (md5('academykb:adoption:st:VT:state_energy:vermont-commercial-building-energy-standards-cbes-')::uuid)::text, '2026-11-22T02:26:12Z'::timestamptz, 'official_text', 'verified', 'https://publicservice.vermont.gov/efficiency/building-energy-standards/commercial-building-energy-standards', '2fd2559165eca4fdd032ca4c08cd878e0f51cca968d64df5286f3fab3e460bfa', 'On April 10, 2026, the Department adopted revisions to the CBES rule which will take effect July 14, 2026 . The new rule allows for compliance with either the 2020 or 2024 CBES.', 'Quote re-checked word for word on the official page by the Academy source check.'),
  ('jurisdiction', 'VT', '2026-11-22T02:26:12Z'::timestamptz, 'official_text', 'verified', 'https://legislature.vermont.gov/statutes/section/20/173/02730', null, '(b) The term “public building” does not include: (1) An owner-occupied single-family residence, unless used for a purpose described in subsection (a) of this section.', 'Statewide code model, re-checked on the official page.'),
  ('adoption', (md5('academykb:adoption:st:WA:ibc:2021')::uuid)::text, '2026-11-22T02:26:12Z'::timestamptz, 'official_text', 'verified', 'https://app.leg.wa.gov/WAC/default.aspx?cite=51-50-003', '15a2ec5c7e24600acc3d7d18f7e5e08feafa88a33a5c63b005a52a361627c9ff', 'The 2021 edition of the International Building Code, including Appendix E, published by the International Code Council is hereby adopted by reference with the exceptions noted in this chapter of the Washington Administrative Code. [Statutory Authority: RCW 19.27.031 and 19.27.074. WSR 22-13-094, 23-12-103, and 23-20-023, § 51-50-003, filed 6/14/22, 6/7/23, and 9/25/23, effective 3/15/24;', 'Quote re-checked word for word on the official page by the Academy source check.'),
  ('adoption', (md5('academykb:adoption:st:WA:iebc:2021')::uuid)::text, '2026-11-22T02:26:12Z'::timestamptz, 'official_text', 'verified', 'https://app.leg.wa.gov/WAC/default.aspx?cite=51-50&full=true', '56dd4557e89aeea6ead965af2b299b99ab856855e02d8993752f7948416a16df', 'The 2021 International Existing Building Code is included in the adoption of this code in Section 101.4.7 and amended in WAC 51-50-480000. [Statutory Authority: RCW 19.27.031 and 19.27.074. WSR 22-13-094, 23-12-103, and 23-20-023, § 51-50-007, filed 6/14/22, 6/7/23, and 9/25/23, effective 3/15/24;', 'Quote re-checked word for word on the official page by the Academy source check.'),
  ('adoption', (md5('academykb:adoption:st:WA:irc:2021')::uuid)::text, '2026-11-22T02:26:12Z'::timestamptz, 'official_text', 'verified', 'https://app.leg.wa.gov/WAC/default.aspx?cite=51-51-003', '31fc1d21810b8cd631c5115016551ba0b36cbe33b07d883613411c7b543c2d9d', 'The 2021 edition of the International Residential Code as published by the International Code Council is hereby adopted by reference with the following additions, deletions, and exceptions: Provided that chapters 11 and 25 through 43 of this code are not adopted.', 'Quote re-checked word for word on the official page by the Academy source check.'),
  ('adoption', (md5('academykb:adoption:st:WA:imc:2021')::uuid)::text, '2026-11-22T02:26:12Z'::timestamptz, 'official_text', 'verified', 'https://app.leg.wa.gov/WAC/default.aspx?cite=51-52-003', '97fe4cd2dfb96ada4bfcc540a5925fd86937cd7b57fc2b6f87d67fe7d3f54bbf', 'The 2021 edition of the International Mechanical Code published by the International Code Council is hereby adopted by reference with the exceptions noted in this chapter of the Washington Administrative Code (WAC). [Statutory Authority: RCW 19.27.031 and 19.27.074. WSR 23-23-105, § 51-52-003, filed 11/15/23, effective 3/16/24; WSR 23-02-055, 23-12-106, and 23-20-025, § 51-52-003, filed 1/3/23, 6/7/23, and 9/25/23, effective 3/15/24;', 'Quote re-checked word for word on the official page by the Academy source check.'),
  ('adoption', (md5('academykb:adoption:st:WA:ifc:2021')::uuid)::text, '2026-11-22T02:26:12Z'::timestamptz, 'official_text', 'verified', 'https://app.leg.wa.gov/WAC/default.aspx?cite=51-54A-003', '93810512cb1530bdb5bad6c6ccf709beb4d66a355de36859233603652a04990a', 'The 2021 edition of the International Fire Code, published by the International Code Council is hereby adopted by reference with the following additions, deletions, and exceptions. [Statutory Authority: RCW 19.27.031 and 19.27.074. WSR 22-13-093, 23-12-107, and 23-20-027, § 51-54A-003, filed 6/14/22, 6/7/23, and 9/25/23, effective 3/15/24;', 'Quote re-checked word for word on the official page by the Academy source check.'),
  ('adoption', (md5('academykb:adoption:st:WA:upc:2021')::uuid)::text, '2026-11-22T02:26:12Z'::timestamptz, 'official_text', 'verified', 'https://app.leg.wa.gov/WAC/default.aspx?cite=51-56-003', 'd7f83d50879f188579775bbf4ed0b2c47618c32efe32c31584d141dc91c21c78', 'The 2021 edition of the Uniform Plumbing Code, including Appendices A, B, I, and M, published by the International Association of Plumbing and Mechanical Officials, is hereby adopted by reference with the following additions, deletions and exceptions: Provided that chapters 12 and 14 of this code are not adopted.', 'Quote re-checked word for word on the official page by the Academy source check.'),
  ('adoption', (md5('academykb:adoption:st:WA:state_energy:2021')::uuid)::text, '2026-11-22T02:26:12Z'::timestamptz, 'official_text', 'verified', 'https://app.leg.wa.gov/WAC/default.aspx?cite=51-11C-10100', '046c848cae69f268a043319050cbd39460a51901c97703c51a494e9715d02eaa', 'The 2021 edition of the Washington State Energy Code is hereby adopted. The Washington State Energy Code adopted under chapter 51-11C WAC shall become effective in all counties and cities of this state on March 15, 2024.', 'Quote re-checked word for word on the official page by the Academy source check.'),
  ('adoption', (md5('academykb:adoption:st:WA:state_energy:2021')::uuid)::text, '2026-11-22T02:26:12Z'::timestamptz, 'official_text', 'verified', 'https://app.leg.wa.gov/WAC/default.aspx?cite=51-11R-10100', '628123a7fcfdd5d1f5b6c01a333702f6bd3b3adc621422ea57906fa399f8c3cf', 'The 2021 edition of the Washington State Energy Code is hereby adopted. The Washington State Energy Code adopted under chapter 51-11R WAC shall become effective in all counties and cities of this state on March 15, 2024. R101.2 Scope. This code applies to residential buildings and the buildings sites and associated systems and equipment. This code shall be the maximum and minimum energy code for residential construction in each town, city and county.', 'Quote re-checked word for word on the official page by the Academy source check.'),
  ('adoption', (md5('academykb:adoption:st:WA:nec:2023')::uuid)::text, '2026-11-22T02:26:12Z'::timestamptz, 'official_text', 'verified', 'https://app.leg.wa.gov/WAC/default.aspx?cite=296-46B-010', '17bc4c06de2d14d89cf3dc8b969be6201f352941f3f1ee2ea0461b9f72556678', '(1) The 2023 edition of the National Electrical Code (NFPA 70 - 2023) including Annex A, B, C, and subsequent Errata and Tentative Interim Amendments issued by the National Fire Protection Association; ... are hereby adopted by reference as part of this chapter. Effective December 31, 2026, the 2026 edition of the National Electrical Code (NFPA 70-2026) including Annex A, B, and C is adopted in this chapter by reference and replaces the 2023 edition of the NFPA 70.', 'Quote re-checked word for word on the official page by the Academy source check.'),
  ('jurisdiction', 'WA', '2026-11-22T02:26:12Z'::timestamptz, 'official_text', 'verified', 'https://app.leg.wa.gov/RCW/default.aspx?cite=19.27.031', null, '(1) Except as otherwise provided in this chapter, there shall be in effect in all counties and cities the state building code which shall consist of the following model codes which are hereby adopted by reference: (a)(i) The International Building Code, published by the International Code Council, Inc.; (ii) The International Residential Code, published by the International Code Council, Inc.;', 'Statewide code model, re-checked on the official page.'),
  ('adoption', (md5('academykb:adoption:st:WI:iecc:2009')::uuid)::text, '2026-11-22T02:26:12Z'::timestamptz, 'official_text', 'verified', 'https://dsps.wi.gov/a-z-programs-list/udc/', '8dceabe9c5463767ac56f184a4116e7b6ae6c46523c0f4113e95edf5fe12d56c', 'Effective January 1, 2016, the Wisconsin Uniform Dwelling Code updated its energy conservation code to the 2009 International Energy Conservation Code.', 'Quote re-checked word for word on the official page by the Academy source check.'),
  ('adoption', (md5('academykb:adoption:st:WI:ibc:2021')::uuid)::text, '2026-11-22T02:26:12Z'::timestamptz, 'official_text', 'verified', 'https://dsps.wi.gov/Pages/Programs/CommercialBuildings/Default.aspx', '125599bad9352795aadc61a5f21529a0180c112fe5497dc06b72badd193a5752', 'DSPS has developed Commercial Building Code inserts for the 2021 IBC, IECC, IMC, IFGC, and IEBC. See the program''s Reference Material page.', 'Quote re-checked word for word on the official page by the Academy source check.'),
  ('adoption', (md5('academykb:adoption:st:WI:iecc:2021')::uuid)::text, '2026-11-22T02:26:12Z'::timestamptz, 'official_text', 'verified', 'https://dsps.wi.gov/a-z-programs-list/electrical/', '76a37c8b2096d946d18ef865b40396eed69fc69fe1c85beface330d88f32c88e', 'Within COMcheck, a user is required to choose the code option of "2021 IECC" unless 2021 IECC section C401.2.2 is applied which would then allow the application of ASHRAE 90.1-2019, in which case the option "90.1 (2019) Standard" must be used.', 'Quote re-checked word for word on the official page by the Academy source check.'),
  ('adoption', (md5('academykb:adoption:st:WI:imc:2021')::uuid)::text, '2026-11-22T02:26:12Z'::timestamptz, 'official_text', 'verified', 'https://dsps.wi.gov/Pages/Programs/CommercialBuildings/Default.aspx', '125599bad9352795aadc61a5f21529a0180c112fe5497dc06b72badd193a5752', 'DSPS has developed Commercial Building Code inserts for the 2021 IBC, IECC, IMC, IFGC, and IEBC. See the program''s Reference Material page.', 'Quote re-checked word for word on the official page by the Academy source check.'),
  ('adoption', (md5('academykb:adoption:st:WI:ifgc:2021')::uuid)::text, '2026-11-22T02:26:12Z'::timestamptz, 'official_text', 'verified', 'https://dsps.wi.gov/Pages/Programs/CommercialBuildings/Default.aspx', '125599bad9352795aadc61a5f21529a0180c112fe5497dc06b72badd193a5752', 'We have received several inquiries about application of the 2021 International Fuel Gas Code (IFGC) as amended by SPS 365.0501(4). The amendment requires all fuel-fired equipment to be provided plastic venting materials that meet UL 1738.', 'Quote re-checked word for word on the official page by the Academy source check.'),
  ('adoption', (md5('academykb:adoption:st:WI:iebc:2021')::uuid)::text, '2026-11-22T02:26:12Z'::timestamptz, 'official_text', 'verified', 'https://dsps.wi.gov/Pages/Programs/CommercialBuildings/Default.aspx', '125599bad9352795aadc61a5f21529a0180c112fe5497dc06b72badd193a5752', 'DSPS has developed Commercial Building Code inserts for the 2021 IBC, IECC, IMC, IFGC, and IEBC. See the program''s Reference Material page.', 'Quote re-checked word for word on the official page by the Academy source check.'),
  ('adoption', (md5('academykb:adoption:st:WI:nec:2023')::uuid)::text, '2026-11-22T02:26:12Z'::timestamptz, 'official_text', 'verified', 'https://dsps.wi.gov/MediaFileLocation/qv4nl4uf/dsps-celebrates-latest-code-update.pdf', 'aa10a1637e30721b3034ced3de13bf66a6af210192f7c5983d59ed210f1109a9', 'September 1, 2026 ... DSPS Celebrates Latest Code Update Wisconsin’s new electrical code takes effect today ... Wisconsin is adopting the 2023 National Electric Code, moving away from using the 2017 edition with amendments.', 'Quote re-checked word for word on the official page by the Academy source check.'),
  ('jurisdiction', 'WI', '2026-11-22T02:26:12Z'::timestamptz, 'official_text', 'verified', 'https://dsps.wi.gov/a-z-programs-list/udc/', null, 'A permit under the UDC is required for new one- and two-family dwelling units. This includes stick-built, modular, and manufactured home installations. Where Can I Get a Permit? If the municipality covering your project location has been delegated authority to issue permits, and the project is not for a state-owned building or land, contact the municipality directly. Use the UDC Delegated Agent List to determine if your municipality has authority to permit and inspect your project. If your municipality does not have the proper authority, submit your application to DSPS via esla.wi.gov .', 'Statewide code model, re-checked on the official page.'),
  ('adoption', (md5('academykb:adoption:st:WY:nec:2026')::uuid)::text, '2026-11-22T02:26:12Z'::timestamptz, 'official_text', 'verified', 'https://wsfm.wyo.gov/electrical-safety/rules-statutes-and-jurisdictions', 'bd9aa649706930d726375407ca7ab7221c3a36df66b83772b852687609e3a875', 'State of Wyoming Adopted Codes The State of Wyoming, on June 28, 2024 adopted the 2024 International Codes. The following codes apply: 2024 International Fire Code 2024 International Building Code 2024 International Fuel & Gas Code 2024 International Mechanical Code 2024 International Existing Building Code 2026 National Electrical Code', 'Quote re-checked word for word on the official page by the Academy source check.'),
  ('jurisdiction', 'WY', '2026-11-22T02:26:12Z'::timestamptz, 'official_text', 'verified', 'https://wyoleg.gov/statutes/compress/title35.pdf', null, '(a) The state fire marshal shall delegate complete authority to municipalities and counties which apply to enforce and interpret local or state fire, building, existing building standards or electrical safety standards which meet the requirements of this section.', 'Statewide code model, re-checked on the official page.'),
  ('source', (md5('academykb:source:ibc-2021')::uuid)::text, '2026-11-22T02:26:12Z'::timestamptz, 'official_text', 'verified', 'https://www.akleg.gov/basis/aac.asp?media=print&secStart=13.50.020&secEnd=13.50.020', 'b4ee43258ec880d982201f9ea45567861b0a781a9b3b04536432f08ca137d795', '13 AAC 50.020. International Building Code. The International Building Code 2021 Edition (IBC), Chapters 1 - 12, 14 - 28, and 30 - 35, and Appendix C are adopted by reference to regulate all occupancies and buildings', 'Edition confirmed by AK''s official adopting text.'),
  ('source', (md5('academykb:source:iebc-2021')::uuid)::text, '2026-11-22T02:26:12Z'::timestamptz, 'official_text', 'verified', 'https://www.akleg.gov/basis/aac.asp?media=print&secStart=13.50.021&secEnd=13.50.021', '8ce0c5cdc815951c936539b00e99035d4c7aab8733abe0db1bdda701a1f9f9d5', '13 AAC 50.021. International Existing Building Code. The International Existing Building Code 2021 Edition (IEBC), Chapters l - 16, and Appendix A - C, are adopted by reference to regulate all occupancies and buildings', 'Edition confirmed by AK''s official adopting text.'),
  ('source', (md5('academykb:source:imc-2021')::uuid)::text, '2026-11-22T02:26:12Z'::timestamptz, 'official_text', 'verified', 'https://www.akleg.gov/basis/aac.asp?media=print&secStart=13.50.023&secEnd=13.50.023', '50d905b39cc72ea0d9b97673fe355fcc86f5c30cee5879fe3df15d2e1d09d4f2', '13 AAC 50.023. International Mechanical Code. The International Mechanical Code 2021 Edition (IMC), Chapters 1 - 15 and Appendix A, are adopted by reference to regulate all occupancies and buildings', 'Edition confirmed by AK''s official adopting text.'),
  ('source', (md5('academykb:source:ifgc-2021')::uuid)::text, '2026-11-22T02:26:12Z'::timestamptz, 'official_text', 'verified', 'https://www.akleg.gov/basis/aac.asp?media=print&secStart=13.50.024&secEnd=13.50.024', '72caab4de5d219490375916b7150dc38f82fa5d5dff99be1d19bb99bf15545fd', '13 AAC 50.024. International Fuel Gas Code. The International Fuel Gas Code 2021 Edition (IFGC), Chapter 3 Section 304 and Chapters 6 and 7, are adopted by reference to regulate the installation of fuel gas utilization equipment, gaseous hydrogen systems, and related accessories', 'Edition confirmed by AK''s official adopting text.'),
  ('source', (md5('academykb:source:ifc-2021')::uuid)::text, '2026-11-22T02:26:12Z'::timestamptz, 'official_text', 'verified', 'https://www.akleg.gov/basis/aac.asp?media=print&secStart=13.50.025&secEnd=13.50.025', '9b6bef10bab619b51ddd4a98ebc39bfddd9739fe603256e2901d2fae277f1385', '13 AAC 50.025. International Fire Code. The International Fire Code 2021 Edition (IFC), Chapters 13 - 19, 41 - 49, and 68 - 79 are reserved. The International Fire Code 2021 Edition (IFC), Chapters 1 - 12, 20 - 40, 50 - 67, and 80 and Appendices B - I, K, L, and N are adopted by reference to regulate all occupancies and buildings', 'Edition confirmed by AK''s official adopting text.'),
  ('source', (md5('academykb:source:nec-2020')::uuid)::text, '2026-11-22T02:26:12Z'::timestamptz, 'official_text', 'verified', 'https://www.akleg.gov/basis/aac.asp?media=print&secStart=8.70.025&secEnd=8.70.025', '2e3996ad0ae39e778af908984da798580d8e307878e4e6fc19cbec4d584ccb86', '8 AAC 70.025. Minimum electrical standards. (a) The 2020 Edition of NFPA 70, National Electrical Code, issued by the National Fire Protection Association on August 5, 2019, and approved by the American National Standards Institute on August 25, 2019, constitutes the minimum electrical code for the state and is adopted by reference.', 'Edition confirmed by AK''s official adopting text.'),
  ('source', (md5('academykb:source:upc-2018')::uuid)::text, '2026-11-22T02:26:12Z'::timestamptz, 'official_text', 'verified', 'https://www.akleg.gov/basis/aac.asp?media=print&secStart=8.63.010&secEnd=8.63.010', '5dbd4f851fc78955dfacc02c43147c9684384cfc2ecb8a98d4fbb6ecbc44323a', 'The codes set out in this section are adopted in accordance with AS 18.60.705 as the minimum plumbing standards to be followed throughout the state, except as provided under AS 18.60.710 or 18.60.735. The department adopts the following codes by reference that are published by the International Association of Plumbing and Mechanical Officials (IAPMO): (1) Uniform Plumbing Code , 2018 edition', 'Edition confirmed by AK''s official adopting text.'),
  ('source', (md5('academykb:source:ipc-2021')::uuid)::text, '2026-11-22T02:26:12Z'::timestamptz, 'official_text', 'verified', 'https://admincode.legislature.state.al.us/api/rule/355-12-1-.01', '99e406e4de56ab063e5a91d296f9ba167e2385ee7d55f470856e3c9716b86806', '(c) 2021 - International Plumbing Code', 'Edition confirmed by AL''s official adopting text.'),
  ('source', (md5('academykb:source:ashrae_90_1-2013')::uuid)::text, '2026-11-22T02:26:12Z'::timestamptz, 'official_text', 'verified', 'https://admincode.legislature.state.al.us/api/rule/355-12-1-.01', '99e406e4de56ab063e5a91d296f9ba167e2385ee7d55f470856e3c9716b86806', '(h) ANSI/ASHRAE/IES Standard 90.1 – 2013 Energy Standard for Buildings except Low–Rise Residential Buildings with exceptions permitted to:', 'Edition confirmed by AL''s official adopting text.'),
  ('source', (md5('academykb:source:ibc-2024')::uuid)::text, '2026-11-22T02:26:12Z'::timestamptz, 'official_text', 'verified', 'https://www.dgs.ca.gov/-/media/Divisions/BSC/05-Resources/Guidebooks/2025-Guide-toTitle-24---6th-Edition.pdf', '955853a2c9726d37a728d5a3bc694f244c280932279717d48cae5612313366f6', '2025 Guide to Title 24: "Part 2 California Building Code, Volumes 1 and 2, based on the 2024 International Building Code" | BSC Codes page: "The 2025 California Building Standards Code (Cal. Code Regs., Title 24) will be published July 1, 2025, with an effective date of January 1, 2026."', 'Edition confirmed by CA''s official adopting text.'),
  ('source', (md5('academykb:source:irc-2024')::uuid)::text, '2026-11-22T02:26:12Z'::timestamptz, 'official_text', 'verified', 'https://www.dgs.ca.gov/-/media/Divisions/BSC/05-Resources/Guidebooks/2025-Guide-toTitle-24---6th-Edition.pdf', '955853a2c9726d37a728d5a3bc694f244c280932279717d48cae5612313366f6', '2025 Guide to Title 24: "Part 2.5 California Residential Code, based on the 2024 International Residential Code" | BSC Codes page: "The 2025 California Building Standards Code (Cal. Code Regs., Title 24) will be published July 1, 2025, with an effective date of January 1, 2026."', 'Edition confirmed by CA''s official adopting text.'),
  ('source', (md5('academykb:source:nec-2023')::uuid)::text, '2026-11-22T02:26:12Z'::timestamptz, 'official_text', 'verified', 'https://www.dgs.ca.gov/-/media/Divisions/BSC/05-Resources/Guidebooks/2025-Guide-toTitle-24---6th-Edition.pdf', '955853a2c9726d37a728d5a3bc694f244c280932279717d48cae5612313366f6', '2025 Guide to Title 24: "Part 3 California Electrical Code, based on the 2023 National Electrical Code" | BSC Codes page: "The 2025 California Building Standards Code (Cal. Code Regs., Title 24) will be published July 1, 2025, with an effective date of January 1, 2026."', 'Edition confirmed by CA''s official adopting text.'),
  ('source', (md5('academykb:source:umc-2024')::uuid)::text, '2026-11-22T02:26:12Z'::timestamptz, 'official_text', 'verified', 'https://www.dgs.ca.gov/-/media/Divisions/BSC/05-Resources/Guidebooks/2025-Guide-toTitle-24---6th-Edition.pdf', '955853a2c9726d37a728d5a3bc694f244c280932279717d48cae5612313366f6', '2025 Guide to Title 24: "Part 4 California Mechanical Code, based on the 2024 Uniform Mechanical Code" | BSC Codes page: "The 2025 California Building Standards Code (Cal. Code Regs., Title 24) will be published July 1, 2025, with an effective date of January 1, 2026."', 'Edition confirmed by CA''s official adopting text.'),
  ('source', (md5('academykb:source:upc-2024')::uuid)::text, '2026-11-22T02:26:12Z'::timestamptz, 'official_text', 'verified', 'https://www.dgs.ca.gov/-/media/Divisions/BSC/05-Resources/Guidebooks/2025-Guide-toTitle-24---6th-Edition.pdf', '955853a2c9726d37a728d5a3bc694f244c280932279717d48cae5612313366f6', '2025 Guide to Title 24: "Part 5 California Plumbing Code, based on the 2024 Uniform Plumbing Code" | BSC Codes page: "The 2025 California Building Standards Code (Cal. Code Regs., Title 24) will be published July 1, 2025, with an effective date of January 1, 2026."', 'Edition confirmed by CA''s official adopting text.'),
  ('source', (md5('academykb:source:ifc-2024')::uuid)::text, '2026-11-22T02:26:12Z'::timestamptz, 'official_text', 'verified', 'https://www.dgs.ca.gov/-/media/Divisions/BSC/05-Resources/Guidebooks/2025-Guide-toTitle-24---6th-Edition.pdf', '955853a2c9726d37a728d5a3bc694f244c280932279717d48cae5612313366f6', '2025 Guide to Title 24: "Part 9 California Fire Code, based on the 2024 International Fire Code" | BSC Codes page: "The 2025 California Building Standards Code (Cal. Code Regs., Title 24) will be published July 1, 2025, with an effective date of January 1, 2026."', 'Edition confirmed by CA''s official adopting text.'),
  ('source', (md5('academykb:source:iebc-2024')::uuid)::text, '2026-11-22T02:26:12Z'::timestamptz, 'official_text', 'verified', 'https://www.dgs.ca.gov/-/media/Divisions/BSC/05-Resources/Guidebooks/2025-Guide-toTitle-24---6th-Edition.pdf', '955853a2c9726d37a728d5a3bc694f244c280932279717d48cae5612313366f6', '2025 Guide to Title 24: "Part 10 California Existing Building Code, based on the 2024 International Existing Building Code" | BSC Codes page: "The 2025 California Building Standards Code (Cal. Code Regs., Title 24) will be published July 1, 2025, with an effective date of January 1, 2026."', 'Edition confirmed by CA''s official adopting text.'),
  ('source', (md5('academykb:source:st:CA:state_energy:2025-california-energy-code-building-energy-effici')::uuid)::text, '2026-11-22T02:26:12Z'::timestamptz, 'official_text', 'verified', 'https://www.energy.ca.gov/programs-and-topics/programs/building-energy-efficiency-standards/2025-building-energy-efficiency', '55a5722e2edbcc2a8bfded8ff792e0f2f4b2ba63e33af69d7d3f1c1191490a57', 'Buildings whose permit applications are applied for on or after January 1, 2026, must comply with the 2025 Energy Code.', 'Confirmed on the official state page.'),
  ('source', (md5('academykb:source:nec-2026')::uuid)::text, '2026-11-22T02:26:12Z'::timestamptz, 'official_text', 'verified', 'https://www.sos.state.co.us/CCR/GenerateRulePdf.do?ruleVersionId=12714&fileName=3%20CCR%20710-1', '44721f9ab741854f528959b2daee171a087f3e9fcd9a61543e22dde631196bfa', 'A. The Board hereby incorporates by reference the National Fire Protection Association standard number 70, hereafter known as the National Electrical Code, 2026 Edition. These standards are incorporated by reference as the minimum standards governing the planning, laying out, and installing or the making of additions, alterations, and repairs in the installation of wiring apparatus and equipment for electric light, heat, and power in this state. This Rule does not include later amendments to or editions of the National Electrical Code, 2026 Edition. The effective date shall be August 1, 2026.', 'Edition confirmed by CO''s official adopting text.'),
  ('source', (md5('academykb:source:ipc-2024')::uuid)::text, '2026-11-22T02:26:12Z'::timestamptz, 'official_text', 'verified', 'https://www.sos.state.co.us/CCR/GenerateRulePdf.do?ruleVersionId=12668&fileName=3%20CCR%20720-1', '1cb44c8ba4348eab14803465ff5295c647fbe42bcaaa092a5a2585969ea2ee0c', '1. Chapter 1, Sections 101.2, 102, 105, 106.1, 106.3, 106.4, 106.5, 106.5.5, 106.6.1, 107, 108.1, 110.3 Chapters 2-13, 15; and Appendices B, C, D, and E of the IPC, 2024 edition promulgated by the International Code Council 1st printing (June 2023). ... Rules 1.2 eff. 08/14/2026.', 'Edition confirmed by CO''s official adopting text.'),
  ('source', (md5('academykb:source:ifgc-2024')::uuid)::text, '2026-11-22T02:26:12Z'::timestamptz, 'official_text', 'verified', 'https://dca.georgia.gov/document/document/new-codes-and-amendments-effective-january-1-2026-memo/download', '050ac9e001d9ae23f6406a427938cd688826d43b2df28a257066b9ead9ce85a5', 'voted to adopt the following codes with an effective date of January 1, 2026: ... 2024 International Fuel Gas Code with Georgia Amendments', 'Edition confirmed by GA''s official adopting text.'),
  ('source', (md5('academykb:source:iecc-2021')::uuid)::text, '2026-11-22T02:26:12Z'::timestamptz, 'official_text', 'verified', 'https://portal.ct.gov/das/-/media/das-beta/pdf/office-of-state-building-inspector/2022-csbc-final.pdf?rev=6b86ccc456024731b3eb61ef0b1c71e1', '6a4f32eabb8e451fae0b6585f132cfae99930246ae0c25236e7eee1023de018a', 'Pursuant to section 29-252 of the Connecticut General Statutes the following national model codes, as amended herein, are adopted and shall be known as the 2022 Connecticut State Building Code: 2021 International Building Code 2017 ICC/ANSI A117.1 Accessible and Usable Buildings and Facilities 2021 International Existing Building Code 2021 International Plumbing Code 2021 International Mechanical Code 2021 International Energy Conservation Code 2020 NFPA 70, National Electrical Code, of the National Fire Protection Association Inc.', 'Edition confirmed by CT''s official adopting text.'),
  ('source', (md5('academykb:source:irc-2021')::uuid)::text, '2026-11-22T02:26:12Z'::timestamptz, 'official_text', 'verified', 'https://portal.ct.gov/das/-/media/das-beta/pdf/office-of-state-building-inspector/2022-csbc-final.pdf?rev=6b86ccc456024731b3eb61ef0b1c71e1', '6a4f32eabb8e451fae0b6585f132cfae99930246ae0c25236e7eee1023de018a', 'Exception: Detached one- and two-family dwellings and multiple single-family dwellings (townhouses) not more than three stories above grade plane in height with a separate means of egress, and their accessory structures not more than three stories above grade plane in height, shall comply with the 2021 International Residential Code portion of the 2022 Connecticut State Building Code.', 'Edition confirmed by CT''s official adopting text.'),
  ('source', (md5('academykb:source:nfpa1-2021')::uuid)::text, '2026-11-22T02:26:12Z'::timestamptz, 'official_text', 'verified', 'https://portal.ct.gov/das/-/media/das-beta/pdf/office-of-state-building-inspector/2022-state-codes/2022-csfpc-integrated-errata-1.pdf?rev=cd6886d617da4c788bdfed007acd5b4f', 'fd4ec463f25e51d67ff9ba589282e0051647b7489040775f086aebeb199fae2e', 'NFPA 1, Fire CodeTM of the National Fire Protection Association, (NFPA 1), 2021 edition, with ANNEXES A, C, and F except as amended, altered or deleted and by the addition of certain provisions as indicated in Section 1.0.2 of this Code.', 'Edition confirmed by CT''s official adopting text.'),
  ('source', (md5('academykb:source:ibc-2015')::uuid)::text, '2026-11-22T02:26:12Z'::timestamptz, 'official_text', 'verified', 'https://dob.dc.gov/node/1613981', '949c930335b09464c7ec6ff46751d4f0719ce131bb95978b28aacfc8db9f9717', 'The 2017 DC Construction Codes consist of the 2015 International Code Council (ICC) family of model codes, the 2014 National Electrical Code, and 2013 ASHRAE 90.1, as amended by the District of Columbia Municipal Regulations (DCMR) Title 12, Sections A through M. The 2017 DC Construction Code takes effect on May 29, 2020.', 'Edition confirmed by DC''s official adopting text.'),
  ('source', (md5('academykb:source:irc-2015')::uuid)::text, '2026-11-22T02:26:12Z'::timestamptz, 'official_text', 'verified', 'https://dob.dc.gov/node/1613981', '949c930335b09464c7ec6ff46751d4f0719ce131bb95978b28aacfc8db9f9717', 'The 2017 DC Construction Codes consist of the 2015 International Code Council (ICC) family of model codes, the 2014 National Electrical Code, and 2013 ASHRAE 90.1, as amended by the District of Columbia Municipal Regulations (DCMR) Title 12, Sections A through M. The 2017 DC Construction Code takes effect on May 29, 2020.', 'Edition confirmed by DC''s official adopting text.'),
  ('source', (md5('academykb:source:iebc-2015')::uuid)::text, '2026-11-22T02:26:12Z'::timestamptz, 'official_text', 'verified', 'https://dob.dc.gov/node/1613981', '949c930335b09464c7ec6ff46751d4f0719ce131bb95978b28aacfc8db9f9717', 'The 2017 DC Construction Codes consist of the 2015 International Code Council (ICC) family of model codes, the 2014 National Electrical Code, and 2013 ASHRAE 90.1, as amended by the District of Columbia Municipal Regulations (DCMR) Title 12, Sections A through M. The 2017 DC Construction Code takes effect on May 29, 2020.', 'Edition confirmed by DC''s official adopting text.'),
  ('source', (md5('academykb:source:ipc-2015')::uuid)::text, '2026-11-22T02:26:12Z'::timestamptz, 'official_text', 'verified', 'https://dob.dc.gov/node/1613981', '949c930335b09464c7ec6ff46751d4f0719ce131bb95978b28aacfc8db9f9717', 'The 2017 DC Construction Codes consist of the 2015 International Code Council (ICC) family of model codes, the 2014 National Electrical Code, and 2013 ASHRAE 90.1, as amended by the District of Columbia Municipal Regulations (DCMR) Title 12, Sections A through M. The 2017 DC Construction Code takes effect on May 29, 2020.', 'Edition confirmed by DC''s official adopting text.'),
  ('source', (md5('academykb:source:imc-2015')::uuid)::text, '2026-11-22T02:26:12Z'::timestamptz, 'official_text', 'verified', 'https://dob.dc.gov/node/1613981', '949c930335b09464c7ec6ff46751d4f0719ce131bb95978b28aacfc8db9f9717', 'The 2017 DC Construction Codes consist of the 2015 International Code Council (ICC) family of model codes, the 2014 National Electrical Code, and 2013 ASHRAE 90.1, as amended by the District of Columbia Municipal Regulations (DCMR) Title 12, Sections A through M. The 2017 DC Construction Code takes effect on May 29, 2020.', 'Edition confirmed by DC''s official adopting text.'),
  ('source', (md5('academykb:source:ifgc-2015')::uuid)::text, '2026-11-22T02:26:12Z'::timestamptz, 'official_text', 'verified', 'https://dob.dc.gov/node/1613981', '949c930335b09464c7ec6ff46751d4f0719ce131bb95978b28aacfc8db9f9717', 'The 2017 DC Construction Codes consist of the 2015 International Code Council (ICC) family of model codes, the 2014 National Electrical Code, and 2013 ASHRAE 90.1, as amended by the District of Columbia Municipal Regulations (DCMR) Title 12, Sections A through M. The 2017 DC Construction Code takes effect on May 29, 2020.', 'Edition confirmed by DC''s official adopting text.'),
  ('source', (md5('academykb:source:ifc-2015')::uuid)::text, '2026-11-22T02:26:12Z'::timestamptz, 'official_text', 'verified', 'https://dob.dc.gov/node/1613981', '949c930335b09464c7ec6ff46751d4f0719ce131bb95978b28aacfc8db9f9717', 'The 2017 DC Construction Codes consist of the 2015 International Code Council (ICC) family of model codes, the 2014 National Electrical Code, and 2013 ASHRAE 90.1, as amended by the District of Columbia Municipal Regulations (DCMR) Title 12, Sections A through M. The 2017 DC Construction Code takes effect on May 29, 2020.', 'Edition confirmed by DC''s official adopting text.'),
  ('source', (md5('academykb:source:iecc-2015')::uuid)::text, '2026-11-22T02:26:12Z'::timestamptz, 'official_text', 'verified', 'https://dob.dc.gov/node/1613981', '949c930335b09464c7ec6ff46751d4f0719ce131bb95978b28aacfc8db9f9717', 'The 2017 DC Construction Codes consist of the 2015 International Code Council (ICC) family of model codes, the 2014 National Electrical Code, and 2013 ASHRAE 90.1, as amended by the District of Columbia Municipal Regulations (DCMR) Title 12, Sections A through M. The 2017 DC Construction Code takes effect on May 29, 2020.', 'Edition confirmed by DC''s official adopting text.'),
  ('source', (md5('academykb:source:nec-2014')::uuid)::text, '2026-11-22T02:26:12Z'::timestamptz, 'official_text', 'verified', 'https://dob.dc.gov/node/1613981', '949c930335b09464c7ec6ff46751d4f0719ce131bb95978b28aacfc8db9f9717', 'The 2017 DC Construction Codes consist of the 2015 International Code Council (ICC) family of model codes, the 2014 National Electrical Code, and 2013 ASHRAE 90.1, as amended by the District of Columbia Municipal Regulations (DCMR) Title 12, Sections A through M. The 2017 DC Construction Code takes effect on May 29, 2020.', 'Edition confirmed by DC''s official adopting text.'),
  ('source', (md5('academykb:source:iecc-2024')::uuid)::text, '2026-11-22T02:26:12Z'::timestamptz, 'official_text', 'verified', 'https://documents.dnrec.delaware.gov/Admin/Orders/Secretarys-Order-No-2026-CCE-0002.pdf', '11452132d0fedf1644c769fbdacb041b8ab86e274ba8b16e932fc9e3d83ce6bb', 'Secretary’s Order No.: 2026-CCE-0002 RE: Approving Final Regulations to Amend 7 DE Admin. Code 2101: Regulations for State Energy Conservation Code Date of Issuance: March 10, 2026 Effective Date of the Amendment: April 11, 2026 ... Promulgation of the revised proposed amendments to 7 DE Admin. Code 2101: Regulations for State Energy Conservation Code will enable the Department to adopt by reference the 2024 IECC for residential buildings, the 2024 IECC/ASHRAE 90.1- 2022 for commercial and high-rise residential buildings, and Appendix RE: EV Charging Infrastructure and Appendix CB: Solar-Ready Zone, with amendments;', 'Edition confirmed by DE''s official adopting text.'),
  ('source', (md5('academykb:source:ashrae_90_1-2022')::uuid)::text, '2026-11-22T02:26:12Z'::timestamptz, 'official_text', 'verified', 'https://documents.dnrec.delaware.gov/Admin/Orders/Secretarys-Order-No-2026-CCE-0002.pdf', '11452132d0fedf1644c769fbdacb041b8ab86e274ba8b16e932fc9e3d83ce6bb', 'Secretary’s Order No.: 2026-CCE-0002 RE: Approving Final Regulations to Amend 7 DE Admin. Code 2101: Regulations for State Energy Conservation Code Date of Issuance: March 10, 2026 Effective Date of the Amendment: April 11, 2026 ... Promulgation of the revised proposed amendments to 7 DE Admin. Code 2101: Regulations for State Energy Conservation Code will enable the Department to adopt by reference the 2024 IECC for residential buildings, the 2024 IECC/ASHRAE 90.1- 2022 for commercial and high-rise residential buildings, and Appendix RE: EV Charging Infrastructure and Appendix CB: Solar-Ready Zone, with amendments;', 'Edition confirmed by DE''s official adopting text.'),
  ('source', (md5('academykb:source:nfpa1-2024')::uuid)::text, '2026-11-22T02:26:12Z'::timestamptz, 'official_text', 'verified', 'https://statefiremarshal.delaware.gov/wp-content/uploads/sites/110/2025/12/2026-DSFPR-update.pdf', '60ef5999406e06b41ed24608a2d21baa9df89ace614b804f2467b8875ba68e1c', 'The State Fire Prevention Commission has recently adopted a new edition of the Delaware State Fire Prevention Regulations, Regulation 701, which becomes effective January 1, 2026. ... Regulation 701, Chapter 7 of the Delaware State Fire Prevention Regulations has a complete list of the NFPA Codes and Standards that will be effective January 1, 2026. Some of the commonly used include: • NFPA 1, Fire Code, 2024 edition.', 'Edition confirmed by DE''s official adopting text.'),
  ('source', (md5('academykb:source:imc-2024')::uuid)::text, '2026-11-22T02:26:12Z'::timestamptz, 'official_text', 'verified', 'https://dca.georgia.gov/document/document/new-codes-and-amendments-effective-january-1-2026-memo/download', '050ac9e001d9ae23f6406a427938cd688826d43b2df28a257066b9ead9ce85a5', 'voted to adopt the following codes with an effective date of January 1, 2026: ... 2024 International Mechanical Code with Georgia Amendments', 'Edition confirmed by GA''s official adopting text.'),
  ('source', (md5('academykb:source:iebc-2018')::uuid)::text, '2026-11-22T02:26:12Z'::timestamptz, 'official_text', 'verified', 'https://dca.georgia.gov/community-assistance/construction-codes/current-state-minimum-codes-construction', '058398fa151ac00dd2236b62b2847ba7ad7dcfff2cc8979680cb94c4588f7ef6', 'Current Permissive Codes as Adopted by DCA International Property Maintenance Code, 2018 Edition, with Georgia Amendments ... International Existing Building Code, 2018 Edition, with Georgia Amendments', 'Edition confirmed by GA''s official adopting text.'),
  ('source', (md5('academykb:source:irc-2018')::uuid)::text, '2026-11-22T02:26:12Z'::timestamptz, 'official_text', 'verified', 'https://ags.hawaii.gov/bcc/files/2021/09/2018StateResidentialCode_20201117rev1.pdf', 'dd50bb0e1f98be39716fca7bbcce076b3fc4f05517ae998020d49765facbce91', 'Adopting the 2018 International Residential Code with Amendments The attached document is the Hawaii State Residential Code as adopted on November 17, 2020 by the State Building Code Council in accordance with HRS 107-24.', 'Edition confirmed by HI''s official adopting text.'),
  ('source', (md5('academykb:source:ibc-2018')::uuid)::text, '2026-11-22T02:26:12Z'::timestamptz, 'official_text', 'verified', 'https://ags.hawaii.gov/bcc/files/2021/09/2018StateBuildingCode_20210817.pdf', '304f88574eceb66626792f124a714e4cdeecc61d4a642e583d997f6a59c3ffe5', 'Adopting the 2018 International Building Code with Amendments The attached document is the Hawaii State Building Code as adopted on April 20, 2021 by the State Building Code Council in accordance with HRS 107-24.', 'Edition confirmed by HI''s official adopting text.'),
  ('source', (md5('academykb:source:iecc-2018')::uuid)::text, '2026-11-22T02:26:12Z'::timestamptz, 'official_text', 'verified', 'https://ags.hawaii.gov/bcc/files/2021/01/soh_bcc_energycode_20201215.pdf', 'dabe1e2007a6a0fb2049435af4c975bfaa7fd844decbefff822ffce8b9e88e98', 'The attached document is the Hawai‘i State Energy Code Amendments to the 2018 IECC as adopted on December 15, 2020 by the State Building Code Council in accordance with HRS 107-24. ... Effective Date: December 15, 2020', 'Edition confirmed by HI''s official adopting text.'),
  ('source', (md5('academykb:source:iecc-2012')::uuid)::text, '2026-11-22T02:26:12Z'::timestamptz, 'official_text', 'verified', 'https://www.legis.iowa.gov/docs/iac/chapter/11-19-2026.481.301.pdf', 'fe15db7f44408859cadaa8d50db81661431ecbe902356b41c03925ec101ca9cd', '481—301.24(103A) Residential energy code. The International Energy Conservation Code – Residential Provisions, 2012 edition, published by the International Code Council, located at www.iccsafe.org, is adopted by reference as the residential energy code of the state of Iowa building code, applicable to residential construction limited to three or fewer stories throughout the state of Iowa', 'Edition confirmed by IA''s official adopting text.'),
  ('source', (md5('academykb:source:imc-2018')::uuid)::text, '2026-11-22T02:26:12Z'::timestamptz, 'official_text', 'verified', 'https://adminrules.idaho.gov/rules/current/24/243970.pdf', '61c864fea77e602cbe97036dd5f939d6aca8749a021c2f6b6b156c26be898562', 'Pursuant to Section 54-5001, Idaho Code, the Board adopts, as the Idaho Mechanical Code, the following international codes with identified amendments: (3-28-23) 01. International Mechanical Code. The 2018 Edition, including appendix A, with the following amendments:', 'Edition confirmed by ID''s official adopting text.'),
  ('source', (md5('academykb:source:ifgc-2018')::uuid)::text, '2026-11-22T02:26:12Z'::timestamptz, 'official_text', 'verified', 'https://adminrules.idaho.gov/rules/current/24/243970.pdf', '61c864fea77e602cbe97036dd5f939d6aca8749a021c2f6b6b156c26be898562', '02. International Fuel Gas Code. The 2018 Edition, including appendices A, B, C, and D, with the following amendments:', 'Edition confirmed by ID''s official adopting text.'),
  ('source', (md5('academykb:source:upc-2015')::uuid)::text, '2026-11-22T02:26:12Z'::timestamptz, 'official_text', 'verified', 'https://adminrules.idaho.gov/rules/current/24/243920.pdf', '8c8531e6c48dc2d0dd12dcfdc77b907b4cd54f417b49362dbc3813ae025402f9', 'Pursuant to Section 54-2601, Idaho Code, the Board adopts, as the Idaho State Plumbing Code (ISPC), the 2015 Uniform Plumbing Code, including Appendices A, B, C, D, E, G, I, J, K and L, with the following amendments: (3-28-23)', 'Edition confirmed by ID''s official adopting text.'),
  ('source', (md5('academykb:source:ifc-2018')::uuid)::text, '2026-11-22T02:26:12Z'::timestamptz, 'official_text', 'verified', 'https://dopl.idaho.gov/wp-content/uploads/2025/06/2025-Updated-Idaho-Adopted-Codes.pdf', '672aef6827dd860d0ec6bd8683240bebf592d4fd4f4d8c7a9e297d92a81f45a4', 'Fire Code (administered by the Idaho State Fire Marshal): 2018 International Fire Code', 'Edition confirmed by ID''s official adopting text.'),
  ('source', (md5('academykb:source:st:IL:ibc:ibc-iebc-current-or-most-recent-preceding-edition-')::uuid)::text, '2026-11-22T02:26:12Z'::timestamptz, 'official_text', 'verified', 'https://cdb.illinois.gov/business/codes/buildingcodesregulations.html', 'b893845507294f1554cd5d3c7899e063df67f5b4a71f852b7d5805d8aa537438', 'Commercial buildings in jurisdictions that have not adopted a building code AND state funded buildings. New or substantially improved buildings: IEBC © and IBC © (1/1/25 Incl. App G., Excl. Ch 11, 13, 29). Current edition or most recent preceeding edition.', 'Confirmed on the official state page.'),
  ('source', (md5('academykb:source:st:IL:nec:nec-current-or-most-recent-preceding-edition-for-c')::uuid)::text, '2026-11-22T02:26:12Z'::timestamptz, 'official_text', 'verified', 'https://cdb.illinois.gov/business/codes/buildingcodesregulations.html', 'b893845507294f1554cd5d3c7899e063df67f5b4a71f852b7d5805d8aa537438', 'Excl. Ch 11, 13, 29). Current edition or most recent preceeding edition. 1 NEC © Current edition or most recent preceeding edition.', 'Confirmed on the official state page.'),
  ('source', (md5('academykb:source:st:IL:irc:irc-under-the-illinois-residential-building-code-a')::uuid)::text, '2026-11-22T02:26:12Z'::timestamptz, 'official_text', 'verified', 'https://cdb.illinois.gov/business/codes/buildingcodesregulations.html', 'b893845507294f1554cd5d3c7899e063df67f5b4a71f852b7d5805d8aa537438', 'Residential buildings in jurisdictions that have not adopted a building code where NOT agreed to by the home purchaser and home builder. New construction: IRC © Current edition. (1/1/24 excluding IV and VII)', 'Confirmed on the official state page.'),
  ('source', (md5('academykb:source:ibc-2012')::uuid)::text, '2026-11-22T02:26:12Z'::timestamptz, 'official_text', 'verified', 'https://www.in.gov/dhs/fire-and-building-safety/fpbsc-rules/', '491968d95c1640b3ba58deedd42f5e2f58470b16685af271b6592f32c793dc26', '675 IAC 13-2.6 2014 Indiana Building Code International Building Code, 2012 Edition, First Printing ANSI A117.1 Accessible and Usable Buildings and Facilities, 2009 Edition, First Printing Currently in Effect Effective: 12/1/2014', 'Edition confirmed by IN''s official adopting text.'),
  ('source', (md5('academykb:source:ipc-2006')::uuid)::text, '2026-11-22T02:26:12Z'::timestamptz, 'official_text', 'verified', 'https://www.in.gov/dhs/fire-and-building-safety/fpbsc-rules/', '491968d95c1640b3ba58deedd42f5e2f58470b16685af271b6592f32c793dc26', '675 IAC 16-1.4 2012 Indiana Plumbing Code International Plumbing Code, 2006 Edition, Second Printing Currently in Effect Effective: 12/24/2012', 'Edition confirmed by IN''s official adopting text.'),
  ('source', (md5('academykb:source:imc-2012')::uuid)::text, '2026-11-22T02:26:12Z'::timestamptz, 'official_text', 'verified', 'https://www.in.gov/dhs/fire-and-building-safety/fpbsc-rules/', '491968d95c1640b3ba58deedd42f5e2f58470b16685af271b6592f32c793dc26', '675 IAC 18-1.6 2014 Indiana Mechanical Code International Mechanical Code, 2012 Edition, First Printing Currently in Effect Effective: 12/1/2014', 'Edition confirmed by IN''s official adopting text.'),
  ('source', (md5('academykb:source:ifgc-2012')::uuid)::text, '2026-11-22T02:26:12Z'::timestamptz, 'official_text', 'verified', 'https://www.in.gov/dhs/fire-and-building-safety/fpbsc-rules/', '491968d95c1640b3ba58deedd42f5e2f58470b16685af271b6592f32c793dc26', '675 IAC 25-3 2014 Indiana Fuel Gas Code International Fuel Gas Code, 2012 Edition, Second Printing Currently in Effect Effective: 12/1/2014', 'Edition confirmed by IN''s official adopting text.'),
  ('source', (md5('academykb:source:ifc-2012')::uuid)::text, '2026-11-22T02:26:12Z'::timestamptz, 'official_text', 'verified', 'https://www.in.gov/dhs/fire-and-building-safety/fpbsc-rules/', '491968d95c1640b3ba58deedd42f5e2f58470b16685af271b6592f32c793dc26', '675 IAC 22-2.5 2014 Indiana Fire Code International Fire Code, 2012 Edition, First Printing Currently in Effect Effective: 12/1/2014', 'Edition confirmed by IN''s official adopting text.'),
  ('source', (md5('academykb:source:ashrae_90_1-2007')::uuid)::text, '2026-11-22T02:26:12Z'::timestamptz, 'official_text', 'verified', 'https://www.in.gov/dhs/fire-and-building-safety/fpbsc-rules/', '491968d95c1640b3ba58deedd42f5e2f58470b16685af271b6592f32c793dc26', '675 IAC 19-4 2010 Indiana Energy Conservation Code ANSI/ASHRAE 90.1 Energy Standard for Buildings Except Low-Rise Residential Buildings, 2007 Edition, I-P Edition Currently in Effect Effective: 5/6/2010', 'Edition confirmed by IN''s official adopting text.'),
  ('source', (md5('academykb:source:ifc-2006')::uuid)::text, '2026-11-22T02:26:12Z'::timestamptz, 'official_text', 'verified', 'https://rules.ks.gov/api/policy-library-public/collections/0ae1e448-f5a1-4e09-9d6d-a488ac7c284a/policies/1ebc02f6-abe2-4127-9e00-a266d7216853/document/390df88f-493d-4a76-b770-67ec7299c0a3', 'bbce5f478cf885fa1ec4a0d621dfeef367470c0e0e371c52a25d9832f199ee04', '(b) international fire code (IFC), international code council, 2006 edition, including the appendices but excluding the following: (1) Chapters 22, 30, 33, 34, 35, 36, and 38;', 'Edition confirmed by KS''s official adopting text.'),
  ('source', (md5('academykb:source:ibc-2006')::uuid)::text, '2026-11-22T02:26:12Z'::timestamptz, 'official_text', 'verified', 'https://rules.ks.gov/api/policy-library-public/collections/0ae1e448-f5a1-4e09-9d6d-a488ac7c284a/policies/1ebc02f6-abe2-4127-9e00-a266d7216853/document/390df88f-493d-4a76-b770-67ec7299c0a3', 'bbce5f478cf885fa1ec4a0d621dfeef367470c0e0e371c52a25d9832f199ee04', '(a) International building code (IBC), international code council, 2006 edition, including the appendices but excluding the references in chapter 35 to NFPA 13, 13D, 13R, 14, 30, 72, 101, and 110;', 'Edition confirmed by KS''s official adopting text.'),
  ('source', (md5('academykb:source:nec-2008')::uuid)::text, '2026-11-22T02:26:12Z'::timestamptz, 'official_text', 'verified', 'https://rules.ks.gov/api/policy-library-public/collections/0ae1e448-f5a1-4e09-9d6d-a488ac7c284a/policies/1ebc02f6-abe2-4127-9e00-a266d7216853/document/390df88f-493d-4a76-b770-67ec7299c0a3', 'bbce5f478cf885fa1ec4a0d621dfeef367470c0e0e371c52a25d9832f199ee04', '(n) national electric code. NFPA standard no. 70, including annexes A, B, C, D, E, F, G, and H, 2008 edition;', 'Edition confirmed by KS''s official adopting text.'),
  ('source', (md5('academykb:source:iecc-2009')::uuid)::text, '2026-11-22T02:26:12Z'::timestamptz, 'official_text', 'verified', 'https://dhbc.ky.gov/Documents/Find%20Currently%20Enforced%20Code.pdf', 'ab2f3968603afd02cc36a854db6f195b677897503656ddbe0909f9354bbce647', '2009 International Energy Conservation Code (for use with residential buildings only- see definition in IECC)', 'Edition confirmed by KY''s official adopting text.'),
  ('source', (md5('academykb:source:nfpa54-2012')::uuid)::text, '2026-11-22T02:26:12Z'::timestamptz, 'official_text', 'verified', 'https://dhbc.ky.gov/Documents/Find%20Currently%20Enforced%20Code.pdf', 'ab2f3968603afd02cc36a854db6f195b677897503656ddbe0909f9354bbce647', '2012 NFPA 54 - National Fuel Gas Code', 'Edition confirmed by KY''s official adopting text.'),
  ('source', (md5('academykb:source:nfpa1-2018')::uuid)::text, '2026-11-22T02:26:12Z'::timestamptz, 'official_text', 'verified', 'https://apps.legislature.ky.gov/law/kar/titles/815/010/060/', 'af290331f42342c1dc9214ddc4466c873c625c1b0f27f8f0c6d3199fb35bbe6d', 'NFPA 1, Uniform Fire Code, 2018 edition, and the NFPA referenced standards included in Chapter 2 of NFPA 1 except: ... 49 Ky.R. 2145; 50 Ky.R. 673; eff 9-26-2023.)', 'Edition confirmed by KY''s official adopting text.'),
  ('source', (md5('academykb:source:st:KY:state_plumbing:kentucky-state-plumbing-law-regulations-code')::uuid)::text, '2026-11-22T02:26:12Z'::timestamptz, 'official_text', 'verified', 'https://dhbc.ky.gov/Documents/Find%20Currently%20Enforced%20Code.pdf', 'ab2f3968603afd02cc36a854db6f195b677897503656ddbe0909f9354bbce647', 'Kentucky State Plumbing Law, Regulations & Code (815 KAR Chapter 20)', 'Confirmed on the official state page.'),
  ('source', (md5('academykb:source:ashrae_90_1-2019')::uuid)::text, '2026-11-22T02:26:12Z'::timestamptz, 'official_text', 'verified', 'https://www.maine.gov/dps/fmo/sites/maine.gov.dps.fmo/files/inline-files/MUBEC%20Standards%20and%20Amendments.pdf', 'cd68a4f42aeed9990f884b2a344f9817dd806b145221dea13171fca81052a543', '2019 ASHRAE 90.1 (Energy Standard for Buildings except Low-Rise Residential Buildings) editions without addenda.', 'Edition confirmed by ME''s official adopting text.'),
  ('source', (md5('academykb:source:upc-2021')::uuid)::text, '2026-11-22T02:26:12Z'::timestamptz, 'official_text', 'verified', 'https://www.sos.state.tx.us/texreg/archive/November132026/Adopted%20Rules/22.EXAMINING%20BOARDS.html', 'c599dacafa2764535ab54d1ec1613ffc1f6207032a029a252890791397154c97', 'The Texas State Board of Plumbing Examiners (Board) adopts the amendment to 22 Texas Administrative Code (TAC), Chapter 367, §367.2 which updates the codes adopted under the authority of Texas Occupations Code, Sec. 1301.255 to the 2021 Uniform Plumbing Code and the 2021 International Plumbing Code. ... Effective date: November 19, 2026', 'Edition confirmed by TX''s official adopting text.'),
  ('source', (md5('academykb:source:nfpa1-2012')::uuid)::text, '2026-11-22T02:26:12Z'::timestamptz, 'official_text', 'verified', 'https://nebraskalegislature.gov/laws/statutes.php?statute=81-503.01', 'cf6a66589305953e27a18d595e63cf1bcc0eddc4cde0f5c23238776e87d07db6', '(2) Not later than July 1, 2019, the rules and regulations adopted and promulgated as part of the State Fire Code shall conform generally to the standards recommended by the National Fire Protection Association, Pamphlet Number 1, known as the Fire Code, 2012 edition, the National Fire Protection Association, Pamphlet Number 101, known as the Life Safety Code, 2012 edition, and associated pamphlets', 'Edition confirmed by NE''s official adopting text.'),
  ('source', (md5('academykb:source:st:NJ:state_plumbing:new-jersey-uniform-construction-code-plumbing-subc')::uuid)::text, '2026-11-22T02:26:12Z'::timestamptz, 'official_text', 'verified', 'https://www.nj.gov/dca/codes/codreg/pdf_regs/njac_5_23_3.pdf', 'b12eebd1b713835217bfd6a98aabd1d272a71c530cdaad232fdf660635ca9c85', 'the Commissioner hereby adopts the Model Code of the International Association of Plumbing and Mechanical Officials, known as "The National Standard Plumbing Code/2024," as the plumbing subcode for New Jersey.', 'Confirmed on the official state page.'),
  ('source', (md5('academykb:source:st:OH:state_residential:residential-code-of-ohio-for-one-two-and-three-fam')::uuid)::text, '2026-11-22T02:26:12Z'::timestamptz, 'official_text', 'verified', 'https://codes.ohio.gov/ohio-administrative-code/rule-4101:8-1-01', 'ee6df687e735b069d13069a157c268fbbb3809da8d1f850bc104befcf7e98f0f', 'The 2018 edition of the “International Residential Code”, first printing, Chapters 2 through 24, 29, and 44 as published by the “International Code Council, Inc.” is used as the basis of this document', 'Confirmed on the official state page.'),
  ('source', (md5('academykb:source:nec-2017')::uuid)::text, '2026-11-22T02:26:12Z'::timestamptz, 'official_text', 'verified', 'https://publications.tnsosfiles.com/rules/0780/0780-02/0780-02-01.20250714.pdf', 'b034ac0cea3f99fc81c7b653df983699aceff5587655e9eece589f601e5af74a', 'those prescribed in the National Electrical Code, 2017 edition, published by the National Fire Protection Association, 1 Batterymarch Park, Quincy, Massachusetts 02169, effective October 1, 2018, except that:', 'Edition confirmed by TN''s official adopting text.'),
  ('source', (md5('academykb:source:irc-2012')::uuid)::text, '2026-11-22T02:26:12Z'::timestamptz, 'official_text', 'verified', 'https://tcss.legis.texas.gov/resources/LG/htm/LG.214.htm', '3b12de334810d8373fa0b045c075d6cee729bfba7a27eb88669e3cafcd527230', 'Sec. 214.212. INTERNATIONAL RESIDENTIAL CODE. (a) To protect the public health, safety, and welfare, the International Residential Code, as it existed on May 1, 2012, is adopted as a municipal residential building code in this state. (b) The International Residential Code applies to all construction, alteration, remodeling, enlargement, and repair of residential structures in a municipality.', 'Edition confirmed by TX''s official adopting text.'),
  ('source', (md5('academykb:source:st:VT:state_energy:vermont-residential-building-energy-standards-rbes')::uuid)::text, '2026-11-22T02:26:12Z'::timestamptz, 'official_text', 'verified', 'https://publicservice.vermont.gov/efficiency/building-energy-standards/residential-building-energy-standards', '2f30bbb2257ec7565d22a325c6875daba2d4cee9bf0709c5f506d215e38deadf', 'The new RBES Rule was adopted on April 10, 2026 with an effective date of July 14, 2026 . These updates allow compliance with either the 2020 or 2024 versions of the RBES. The changes provide much needed flexibility and cost reduction opportunities, to help address Vermont’s significant housing shortage. The 2020 and 2024 RBES apply to all new residential construction, including additions, alterations, renovations, and repairs.', 'Confirmed on the official state page.'),
  ('source', (md5('academykb:source:st:VT:state_energy:vermont-commercial-building-energy-standards-cbes-')::uuid)::text, '2026-11-22T02:26:12Z'::timestamptz, 'official_text', 'verified', 'https://publicservice.vermont.gov/efficiency/building-energy-standards/commercial-building-energy-standards', '2fd2559165eca4fdd032ca4c08cd878e0f51cca968d64df5286f3fab3e460bfa', 'On April 10, 2026, the Department adopted revisions to the CBES rule which will take effect July 14, 2026 . The new rule allows for compliance with either the 2020 or 2024 CBES.', 'Confirmed on the official state page.'),
  ('source', (md5('academykb:source:st:WA:state_energy:washington-state-energy-code-commercial-provisions')::uuid)::text, '2026-11-22T02:26:12Z'::timestamptz, 'official_text', 'verified', 'https://app.leg.wa.gov/WAC/default.aspx?cite=51-11C-10100', '046c848cae69f268a043319050cbd39460a51901c97703c51a494e9715d02eaa', 'The 2021 edition of the Washington State Energy Code is hereby adopted. The Washington State Energy Code adopted under chapter 51-11C WAC shall become effective in all counties and cities of this state on March 15, 2024.', 'Confirmed on the official state page.'),
  ('source', (md5('academykb:source:st:WA:state_energy:washington-state-energy-code-residential-provision')::uuid)::text, '2026-11-22T02:26:12Z'::timestamptz, 'official_text', 'verified', 'https://app.leg.wa.gov/WAC/default.aspx?cite=51-11R-10100', '628123a7fcfdd5d1f5b6c01a333702f6bd3b3adc621422ea57906fa399f8c3cf', 'The 2021 edition of the Washington State Energy Code is hereby adopted. The Washington State Energy Code adopted under chapter 51-11R WAC shall become effective in all counties and cities of this state on March 15, 2024. R101.2 Scope. This code applies to residential buildings and the buildings sites and associated systems and equipment. This code shall be the maximum and minimum energy code for residential construction in each town, city and county.', 'Confirmed on the official state page.')
